window.ANSWER_MARKUP={"L01": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["I’m sorry for those words I said.", "I didn’t realize that I hurt your feelings.", "Tina’s white dress was ruined when she spilled a glass of red wine on it.", "The airplane’s test flight ended in failure when it crashed to the ground.", "Every year, we hold a party on our grandfather’s birthday.", "It is a tradition in our family.", "When Sean’s grandmother saw some old family photos, she recalled the days of World War II.", "Sally didn’t reply when I asked her what time she would come back home.", "Instead, she just left without saying a word.", "Before he starts his class, the teacher always does a roll call to see if anyone is skipping class.", "After George met his old school friend accidentally at the park, they happily chatted about their memories for hours.", "Eric is a nice person.", "He always considers other people’s feeling and tries not to upset them in any way.", "The old building reminded Benjamin of the good old days when he was a kid."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["My grandmother is fortunate to be in such good health at her age.", "Linda was surprised to see how tired she looked when she saw her reflection in the mirror.", "Sara has been feeling depressed lately, so I am going to visit her and try to cheer her up.", "At the meeting, the marketing team presented a good plan to attract more buyers.", "Kim memorized all the English words on the list in twenty minutes, but she forgot most of them just as quickly."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["We all know that the Earth is round.", "David was very sad that he was kicked off the school baseball team.", "Jack was angry that his parents were too busy with the other kids to keep an eye on him.", "I’m very sure that it won’t rain, but I’ll still bring my umbrella.", "You should buy the dress because it looks good on you.", "Kenting National Park sounds like a wonderful place for a vacation.", "The cookies you made taste great. Can I have another one?", "We felt excited about taking our first trip to the town. It was very enjoyable.", "Standing in line for a whole night just to take pictures or shake hands with a famous singer sounds pretty crazy to me."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">We all know that the Earth is round</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">David was very sad that he was kicked off the school baseball team</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Jack was angry that his parents were too busy with the other kids to keep an eye</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">on him</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I’m very sure that it won’t rain, but I’ll still bring my umbrella</strong>.", null, "1.\tYou should buy the dress because it (<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">looks</strong> / looks like) good on you.", "2.\tKenting National Park (sounds / <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">sounds like</strong>) a wonderful place for a vacation.", "3.\tThe cookies you made (<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">taste</strong> / taste like) great. Can I have another one?", "4.\tWe felt (<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">excited</strong> / exciting) about taking our first trip to the town. It was very enjoyable.", "5.\tStanding in line for a whole night just to take pictures or shake hands with a famous singer sounds pretty (<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">crazy</strong> / crazily) to me."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["David’s remarks were nothing but a joke; don’t take them too seriously .", "Don’t let your parents down , for they have sacrificed a lot to bring you up.", "The careless rider was badly hurt in the accident and had to walk with the aid of an artificial leg for the rest of his life.", "The cake smelled bad, so I didn’t eat it.", "I think (that) you should be careful before you enjoy any food.", "Mandy got a haircut last week. She looks great with short hair.", "Tina was surprised (that) her ex-boyfriend got married soon after they broke up."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The cake smelled bad, so I didn’t eat it</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I think (that) you should be careful before you enjoy any food</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Mandy got a haircut last week. She looks great with short hair</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Tina was surprised (that) her ex-boyfriend got married soon after they broke up</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["Let’s talk about this whole online learning thing.", "It’s happening more and more often, and you need to make the most out of it.", "Here are <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) a few</strong> tips to help you have the best online learning experience.", "Create a Study Space.", "First off, find a spot to study where you feel <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) comfortable</strong>.", "If there are other people around, then <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) of course</strong> you will want headphones.", "Keep your study things in order, too.", "It saves you from wasting time looking for things.", "Follow a Schedule.", "Speaking of time, it can be very helpful to have a routine.", "You will have a lot to do for your class, and you need to finish them one by one.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) However</strong>, you need to set some limits.", "Breaks are necessary to help your brain relax.", "You can let your body relax too with some quick exercises <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (C) while</strong> you’re taking your break.", "Stay Connected.", "Online learners sometimes say <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) that</strong> they miss talking to people, so keep communicating.", "Don’t be <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) embarrassed</strong> about asking your teachers questions.", "Your classmates can help, too.", "You can use online tools to chat and work together.", "Just <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) make sure</strong> you are clear and polite when talking online.", "Misunderstandings can happen more easily online than <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) in person</strong>.", "To sum up: find the <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (B) perfect</strong> study spot, stick to a routine, and reach out when you need support.", "Good luck!"], "questions": [], "source": ["Let’s talk about this whole online learning thing. It’s happening more and more often, and you need to make the most out of it. Here are   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) a few</strong>   tips to help you have the best online learning experience.", "Create a Study Space. First off, find a spot to study where you feel   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) comfortable</strong>  . If there are other people around, then   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) of course</strong>   you will want headphones. Keep your study things in order, too. It saves you from wasting time looking for things.", "Follow a Schedule*. Speaking of time, it can be very helpful to have a routine*. You will have a lot to do for your class, and you need to finish them one by one.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) However</strong>  , you need to set some limits. Breaks are necessary to help your brain relax. You can let your body relax too with some quick exercises   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (C) while</strong>   you’re taking your break.", "Stay Connected. Online learners sometimes say   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) that</strong>   they miss talking to people, so keep communicating*. Don’t be   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) embarrassed</strong>   about asking your teachers questions. Your classmates can help, too. You can use online tools to chat and work together. Just   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) make sure</strong>", null, "online than   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) in person</strong>  .", "To sum up: find the   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (B) perfect</strong>   study spot, stick to a routine, and reach out when you need support. Good luck!", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["Delivering a successful group presentation can feel like a major challenge.", "In particular, differences in opinions and personalities among group members can get in the way of teamwork and even completely <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (D) ruin</strong> a presentation.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (G) In fact</strong>, certain strategies can help you achieve full group agreement before your presentation.", "Let’s look at a few of these strategies.", "First, define roles and responsibilities.", "Before you begin planning your presentation, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (J) make sure</strong> that everyone in your group has set tasks to complete.", "In this way, each member can clearly <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (F) realize</strong> their role in the planning process.", "Next, practice.", "While planning what you will <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (A) present</strong>, practice your delivery frequently.", "By doing so, you can make certain that you will <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (H) recall</strong> what to say on the actual day.", "You and your team members can help one another by attending practice sessions <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (E) in person</strong> and providing helpful comments during these sessions.", "Third, use visual aids.", "The success of any presentation, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) of course</strong>, relies on not only powerful words but also an effective visual element.", "Consider preparing a PowerPoint presentation that is <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (I) full</strong> of eye-catching images to go with your speech.", "By using these strategies, you will increase your chances of delivering a(n) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (B) memorable</strong> group presentation.", "With careful planning and cooperation among all group members, your presentation is sure to steal the show!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "Delivering a successful group presentation can feel like a major challenge. In particular, differences in opinions and personalities among group members can get in the way of teamwork and even completely   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (D) ruin</strong>   a presentation.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (G) in fact</strong>  , certain strategies* can help you achieve full group agreement before your presentation. Let’s look at a few of these strategies.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (J) make sure</strong>   that everyone in your group has set tasks to complete. In this way, each member can clearly   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (F) realize</strong>   their role in the planning process. Next, practice. While planning what you will   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (A) present</strong>  , practice your delivery frequently. By doing so, you can make certain that you will   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (H) recall</strong>   what to say on the actual day. You and your team members can help one another by attending practice sessions*   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (E) in person</strong>   and providing helpful comments during these sessions. Third, use visual* aids. The success of any presentation,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) of course</strong>  , relies on not only powerful words but also an effective visual element. Consider preparing a PowerPoint presentation that is   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (I) full</strong>   of eye-catching images to go with your speech.", "By using these strategies, you will increase your chances of delivering a(n)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (B) memorable</strong>", null, null, null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["I will never forget my first week of high school.", "Since elementary school, I had been a good basketball player, so I was excited to show off my skills to my new friends.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (D) On the first day of high school, however, I found out that I was not nearly as skilled as my new classmates</strong>.", "This realization came during our first lunchtime match.", "I created a team with some of my classmates and challenged another team to a three-on-three game.", "I ran and shot the ball with all my strength, but the other team easily defeated us.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (B) I felt embarrassed and sad, for I had confidently told my friends how good I was</strong>.", "However, I think these feelings then motivated me to train harder.", "After that first day, I practiced with my friends during every break time for the rest of the week.", "Our skills got better and better, and we learned how to work closely together as a team.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) The next week, we challenged the same team that had beaten us to another game</strong>.", "This time, we were prepared.", "We ended up beating them by two points just before the bell rang for class!", "I learned a valuable life lesson from those two games: No matter how good you think you are, always stay humble.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) There are always stronger competitors, so it is important to learn from them in order to improve yourself</strong>.", "Since then, I have always kept this lesson in mind, and it has helped me through many challenges."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, "I will never forget my first week of high school. Since elementary school, I had been a good basketball player, so I was excited to show off my skills to my new friends.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (D) On the first day of high school, however, I found out that I was not nearly as skilled as my new classmates.</strong>", "This realization came during our first lunchtime match. I created a team with some of my classmates and challenged another team to a three-on-three game. I ran and shot the ball with all my strength, but the other team easily defeated* us.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (B) I felt embarrassed and sad, for I had confidently told my friends how good I was.</strong>   However, I think these feelings then motivated* me to train harder. After that first day, I practiced with my friends during every break time for the rest of the week. Our skills got better and better, and we learned how to work closely together as a team.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) The next week, we challenged the same team that had beaten us to another game.</strong>   This time, we were prepared. We ended up beating them by two points just before the bell rang for class! I learned a valuable life lesson from those two games: No matter how good you think you are, always stay humble.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) There are always stronger competitors, so it is important to learn from them in order to improve yourself.</strong>   Since then, I have always kept this lesson in mind, and it has helped me through many challenges.", null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["Mark’s lifelong dream of traveling abroad finally came true with a trip to Italy this summer.", "Preparing for the trip was an exciting task.", "He got his passport, learned basic Italian phrases, and planned visits to some famous tourist spots.", "On the plane for Italy, Mark was in high spirits.", "The long flight did little to reduce his excitement.", "As he landed in Rome, he couldn’t wait to look around the city, but he soon realized that overcoming the language problem would be quite a challenge.", "Though he had studied some Italian at home, using it in real conversations with native speakers was not easy.", "Despite this, the friendly and patient locals made him feel more at ease.", "Italian food, too, soon made him feel at home.", "In fact, the wonderful meals were probably the best part of Mark’s trip.", "He tasted traditional pizzas and gelato, and he also learned that in Italy, dining is not only about the food but also about spending time and talking with others.", "In addition, historical sites gave him lots of food for thought.", "Visiting the Colosseum and the Vatican was like stepping into history.", "Mark was awestruck by the building designs and the rich stories of these ancient places.", "Also, Pompeii, with its well-kept ruins, offered a unique look into everyday life all those many years ago.", "This journey to Italy was far more than just a vacation for Mark; it was a life-changing experience.", "He learned to deal with new situations, communicate in a completely foreign language, and appreciate different cultures.", "The trip not only broadened his horizons but also left him eager for more adventures abroad."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the purpose of this passage?", "(A) To show how amazing Mark is.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) To describe a memorable trip Mark took.</strong>", "(C) To help readers learn more about Italy.", "(D) To offer useful information about traveling abroad.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following is closest in meaning to the word “awestruck” in the fourth paragraph?", "(A) bored", "(B) depressed", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) surprised</strong>", "(D) embarrassed", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t3.\tAccording to the passage, which of the following is NOT true?", "(A) Mark had some trouble communicating with Italians.", "(B) The trip helped open Mark’s eyes to the big wide world.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) Mark liked ancient Italian buildings best during the journey.</strong>", "(D) Before this trip, Mark had dreamed of traveling abroad for some time."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["To all high school freshmen, three things are important for sure: studies, friendship, and interests.", "Students are introduced to their studies in their classes.", "Outside of their classrooms, they find that joining a club is an excellent way to make new friends and develop interests.", "Students at Power High School have to fill out the club information form below to apply for membership to clubs.", "Please read the following form and answer the questions.", "Power High School Chinese Yo-Yo Club Member’s Information, 2024", "Last Name", "First Name", "Nickname", "Student ID No.", "Pink", "Peppa", "Pinkie", "1800032", "Gender", "Date of Birth", "Place of Birth", "Blood Type", "Female", "Jan. 28, 2008", "Paradiso City", "AB", "Do you have any siblings at Power High School?", "Yes □ No", "Siblings’ name(s): 1. Pippi Pink; 2. Poppo Pink"], "questions": ["For freshmen at Power High School who want to join a club that they are \n(1)  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">interested</strong>   in, (2)    <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">filling</strong>    out a club information form is a must.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are true for Peppa Pink. \n      <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">D F</strong>", "(A) She is a member of the Chinese Chess Club.", "(B) She is a junior high school student.", "(C) Her family name is Peppa.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) Her friends may call her Pinkie.</strong>", "(E) In September 2025, she will be nineteen years old.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(F) She was born in Paradiso City.</strong>", "3.\tWhich word in the information form means “brothers or sisters”? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">siblings</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "L02": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["If you ignore traffic lights, you may get a ticket.", "The students gave their full attention to what the teacher was saying.", "Jason connected the blue wire with the red one, and the phone worked again!", "Since Mr. Chang was not in his office, I left a message for him with his secretary.", "We introduced ourselves to our foreign friends in English and asked where they were staying.", "You won’t know what the man is talking about unless you really focus on his speech.", "If you want to win the girl’s heart, be sure to dress smartly, bring her a small gift, and be polite throughout dinner.", "After a week of hard work, the manager plans to go to a quiet place for a few days to refresh herself.", "The students spent a lot of time preparing for the contest but only got sixth place.", "They were disappointed by the result.", "Many married couples find it hard to maintain the romantic feeling they enjoyed in the early years of marriage."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["The teacher nodded with satisfaction after our group finished the tough job.", "Sheila was Elvis’s inspiration for this song.", "He wrote the song after he met her.", "I sent the food company some e-mails complaining about their goods, but I haven’t gotten any response yet.", "Today, we’ll discuss the problem of food waste, which bears some relationship to the movie we saw last week.", "Jane feels it is difficult to communicate with her boss because he rarely gives her a chance to express her ideas."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["It is useful to learn a second language.", "It is not easy to put this toy together.", "It is impossible for me to finish this history project by the end of the month.", "It is dangerous to ride a motorcycle without wearing a helmet.", "I haven’t seen Judy recently.", "The weather has been rainy and cloudy for the last few days. I hope it will clear up soon.", "Gloria’s online business is doing well, so she has made a lot of money so far this year.", "I haven’t heard from Mr. Chang since he went to Japan last July.", "Jason is sure that he will win the game, for he has beaten this opponent several times before."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is useful to learn a second language</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is not easy to put this toy together</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is impossible for me to finish this history project by the end of the month</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is dangerous to ride a motorcycle without wearing a helmet</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I haven’t seen Judy recently</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The weather has been rainy and cloudy for the last few days. I hope it will clear</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">up soon</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Gloria’s online business is doing well, so she has made a lot of money so far this</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">year</strong>.", null, "I haven’t <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">heard from Mr. Chang since he went to Japan last July</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Jason is sure that he will win the game, for he has beaten this opponent several</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">times before</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["Mr. Wang isn’t poor. In fact , he is the richest person in town.", "Olivia is going through all her food magazines, trying to find a recipe that she saw before.", "Put two-thirds of the money in your pocket in case your luggage gets lost.", "As/Since/Because I have many things to do, I have to turn to my friends (for help).", "We should pay attention in class. In addition, we should review the/our lessons again and again.", "It has been two years since I last saw Nina at the class reunion.", "I miss her a lot, and it is hard for me to forget all the happy times we had together."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">As/Since/Because I have many things to do, I have to turn to my friends (for help</strong>).", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">We should pay attention in class. In addition, we should review the/our lessons again\t\nand again</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It has been two years since I last saw Nina at the class reunion</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I miss her a lot, and it is hard for me to forget all the happy times we had together</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["Many people enjoy playing video games.", "For most, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) playing</strong> games is a relaxing and harmless pastime.", "However, some people may develop a dangerous addiction to gaming.", "If you think <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) that</strong> you or someone you care about has a video game addiction, here are some signs to check for.", "When players keep needing a longer time to get the same feeling of satisfaction, it often means they are becoming addicted.", "This may cause them to stay up late <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) into</strong> the night playing games.", "Thus, addicted gamers may start having problems keeping up with work or school because they’re so busy <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) playing</strong> games.", "In addition, they might also have difficulty concentrating, and their grades are likely to <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (B) get</strong> worse.", "Another way <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) to identify</strong> addiction is to look for problems with the player’s moods and health.", "They may start to become anxious or feel angry or depressed.", "Also, they might lose their appetite, sleep poorly at night, or spend less time <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (C) interacting</strong> with friends and family.", "If someone is addicted, it can be very hard for him or her to stop <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) playing</strong> video games.", "If someone is <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) truly</strong> addicted to video games, the best thing for him or her to do is to see a mental health counselor.", "Such a professional can help people <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (C) change</strong> their behavior and restore a balance in their life.", "If you or someone you love is facing this kind of problem, be sure to get help!"], "questions": [], "source": ["Many people enjoy playing video games. For most,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) playing</strong>   games is a relaxing and harmless pastime. However, some people may develop a dangerous addiction to gaming. If you think   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) that</strong>   you or someone you care about has a video game addiction, here are some signs to check for.", "When players keep needing a longer time to get the same feeling of satisfaction, it often means they are becoming addicted. This may cause them to stay up late   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) into</strong>   the night playing games. Thus, addicted gamers may start having problems keeping up with work or school because they’re so busy   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) playing</strong>   games. In addition, they might also have difficulty concentrating, and their grades are likely to   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (B) get</strong>   worse.", "Another way   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) to identify</strong>   addiction is to look for problems with the player’s moods and health. They may start to become anxious or feel angry or depressed. Also, they might lose their appetite, sleep poorly at night, or spend less time   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (C) interacting</strong>   with friends and family.", "If someone is addicted, it can be very hard for him or her to stop   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) playing</strong>   video games. If someone is   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) truly</strong>   addicted to video games, the best thing for him or her to do is to see a mental health counselor. Such a professional* can help people   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (C) change</strong>   their behavior and restore a balance in their life. If you or someone you love is facing this kind of problem, be sure to get help!", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["Have you ever wanted a boyfriend or girlfriend?", "Do you think it’s good to be in a(n) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) relationship</strong> while you are still in school?", "You might have heard some people suggest that students should not get involved in <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) romantic</strong> relationships at a young age because they are not mature enough to know what they really want from a relationship.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (G) In fact</strong>, that was exactly what happened to me.", "In the beginning, I wanted my first boyfriend to pay <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (J) attention</strong> to me all the time.", "We used to chat every night, and we wanted to spend every minute of the day <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (E) with</strong> each other.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (B) However</strong>, it wasn’t long before I started to change my mind.", "Soon, I wanted to have more time to <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (H) focus</strong> on my studies and other activities.", "Eventually, we broke up, and I was very <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) disappointed</strong> in myself for hurting his feelings so much.", "Even so, I still think it was a good decision.", "As a result, I didn’t get involved with anyone else while I was in school.", "Instead, I found <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (I) satisfaction</strong> in my own interests and hobbies.", "I hope my story can <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (F) inspire</strong> you to explore and learn more about yourself before you start to date someone.", "After all, if you want to get the most out of a relationship, you need to get to know yourself first!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) relationship</strong>   while you are still in school? You might have heard some people suggest that students should not get involved in   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) romantic</strong>   relationships at a young age because they are not mature enough to know what they really want from a relationship.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (G) in fact</strong>  , that was exactly what happened to me. In the beginning, I wanted my first boyfriend to pay   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (J) attention</strong>   to me all the time. We used to chat every night, and we wanted to spend every minute of the day   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (E) with</strong>   each other.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (B) however</strong>  , it wasn’t long before I started to change my mind. Soon, I wanted to have more time to   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (H) focus</strong>   on my studies and other activities. Eventually, we broke up, and I was very   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) disappointed</strong>   in myself for hurting his feelings so much. Even so, I still think it was a good decision. As a result, I didn’t get involved with anyone else while I was in school. Instead, I found   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (I) satisfaction</strong>   in my own interests and hobbies. I hope my story can   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (F) inspire</strong>   you to explore and learn more about yourself before you start to date someone. After all, if you want to get the most out of a relationship, you need to get to know yourself first!", null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["Dear best friend, I know this news will sadden you, but please understand that I have no choice.", "We first met around Christmas time two years ago, and we have had a wonderful time together ever since.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (E) You have helped me come out of my shell, communicate better with others, and make more friends</strong>.", "Also, you have enabled me to experience imaginary worlds and told me such interesting stories.", "Every afternoon after school, we played together in so many different settings, such as at MLB baseball games and through adventures in the jungle.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) Doing all these things with you helped me forget about all the stress of school and made me believe I was doing the right thing</strong>.", "However, as time went by, things started to get worse.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) We were spending so much time together that I began to neglect my family</strong>.", "I would even be in a bad mood whenever my parents forced me to stop playing with you, and I would end up arguing with them.", "What’s worse, you kept persuading me not to do my homework, and my grades got worse.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) This is not the way a student should spend his or her time, my dear Xbox</strong>.", "Therefore, to put things right and to allow me to have a brighter future, I have to throw you away.", "I truly hope you understand.", "Your friend, Adam"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, "I know this news will sadden you, but please understand that I have no choice. We first met around Christmas time two years ago, and we have had a wonderful time together ever since.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (E) You have helped me come out of my shell, communicate better with others, and make more friends.</strong>   Also, you have enabled me to experience imaginary* worlds and told me such interesting stories. Every afternoon after school, we played together in so many different settings, such as at MLB baseball games and through adventures in the jungle.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) Doing all these things with you helped me forget about all the stress of school and made me believe I was doing the right thing.</strong>   However, as time went by, things started to get worse.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) We were spending so much time together that I began to neglect my family.</strong>   I would even be in a bad mood whenever my parents forced me to stop playing with you, and I would end up arguing with them. What’s worse, you kept persuading me not to do my homework, and my grades got worse.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) This is not the way a student should spend his or her time, my dear Xbox.</strong>   Therefore, to put things right and to allow me to have a brighter future, I have to throw you away. I truly hope you understand.", null, null, null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["As cellphones become smarter, they also become more useful.", "We can now take pictures, play games, browse the Internet, buy plane tickets, and much more.", "We spend more and more time glued to our hand-held devices.", "The more things we can do with them, the harder it becomes to put them down.", "What has made us addicted to our phones?", "Here are some factors.", "One of the reasons why we become addicted to smartphones is the apps.", "Apps let us send instant messages to our friends.", "Throughout the day, we keep checking our phones to see if we have gotten replies to messages we have sent or if someone has “liked” a photo we have shared.", "When we don’t see any reply, we get impatient and sometimes even angry.", "Nevertheless, we can’t stop ourselves from checking.", "Another factor is the inconvenience of computers.", "Most of us now have computers at home.", "When we are out of the house, we simply can’t use them.", "But smartphones?", "We take them everywhere.", "Go anywhere, and you will see whole groups of people sitting together.", "They’re all on their phones, not even talking to each other.", "Smartphones have changed our lives for the better in some ways, but they have their drawbacks, too.", "For the most part, checking our phones once in a while is not a big deal.", "However, there are also times when we should interact with the people around us.", "The most important thing to remember is this: Pay more attention to the people around you."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ D ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the main idea of the first paragraph?", "(A) The cost of a cellphone call is getting higher now.", "(B) There are several stages in the history of cellphones.", "(C) One reason why people are addicted to cellphones is the apps.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) The more functions cellphones have, the more time people spend on them.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ A ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following statements is true?", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(A) People are often seen using their cellphones when they get together.</strong>", "(B) It is quite easy for people to break their addiction to their cellphones.", "(C) People use their computers for all kinds of things, even outside their homes.", "(D) People seldom pay attention to whether they get any replies to their messages.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t3.\tWhat is the purpose of the last paragraph?", "(A) To let people know how useful cellphones are.", "(B) To warn people not to use electronic devices too often.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) To remind people to pay more attention to those around them.</strong>", "(D) To encourage people to interact with others through cellphones."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["Addicted to LOL", "Several times I went to you, but you were not home", "All the time I stayed with you", "You were playing LOL", "They told me “hero or enemy” is your new role", "And I know you’re not in my league anymore", "Your mind is not your own", "Your heart beats, your finger moves", "Another phone is what it takes", "You can&#x27;t sleep, you can&#x27;t eat", "There&#x27;s no doubt, you&#x27;re in deep online", "Your throat is tight, you can&#x27;t breathe", "I thought that you could stay away from that stuff", "The truth is you couldn&#x27;t get enough", "I know I have to face it, you&#x27;re addicted to it", "It’s me from whom you stay away", "LOL is the name of an online game, “League of Legends.”"], "questions": ["The writer used the poem to talk about the signs of gaming (1)  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">addiction</strong>   and his/her feelings and (2)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">thoughts</strong>    about the “you” in the poem.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are true for the “you” in the poem. \n      <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">D E</strong>", "(A) The “you” couldn’t be with the “I” as the “you” had to see a doctor.", "(B) The “you” needs only one phone to play LOL.", "(C) The “you” can’t fall asleep and eat well because of a sore throat.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) The “you” could be an ex-friend of the “I.”</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(E) Being addicted to LOL changed the relationship between the “you” and the “I.”</strong>", "(F) The “you” and the “I” were friends in League of Legends.", "3.\tWhat is “that stuff” mentioned in the poem? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">LOL/League of Legends</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "L03": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["Since you didn’t come to the party, I wondered where you were.", "My family went on a long journey by train across the country last week.", "The lights in John’s room are on; I guess he is still awake at this late hour.", "Jessica likes to watch the clouds floating across the sky on sunny days.", "The man is lucky enough to have survived the plane crash; almost all of the other passengers died.", "If you are nervous about the tennis match, you should breathe slowly and try to relax.", "Jennifer is an expert at teaching little children.", "No wonder kids love her so much.", "John didn’t feel well this morning; therefore, he decided to take sick leave and go home for a rest.", "A spider is a small creature with eight legs.", "It makes webs to catch insects for food.", "Cindy received a surprise visit from someone whom she had deliberately avoided for many years."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["The children stared at the magician in amazement when he suddenly pulled a rabbit out of his hat.", "The wonderful scenery in the countryside impressed me so much that I will never forget it.", "Just as he was about to give up any hope of being saved, the sailor saw a boat in the distance.", "Wendy likes to go to the ice cream store, for there are various flavors of ice cream to choose from.", "The average age of the workers at this company is thirty-five, so you are probably the youngest one here."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["The expert wants to know how the young man could solve the problem so easily.", "Eric is wondering why Rachel left him without saying a word.", "Peter’s friends are not sure when his birthday party will be held.", "Nick is asking where the best place to spend time downtown is.", "Jean couldn’t decide what she should give her husband for Christmas.", "English is spoken (by people) in many places.", "A novel will be published by that writer next year.", "All the old furniture on the sidewalk was taken away (by someone) last night.", "Mike has been employed as a handyman by Mrs. Smith for the past three years."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The expert wants to know how the young man could solve the problem so easily</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Eric is wondering why Rachel left him without saying a word</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Peter’s friends are not sure when his birthday party will be held</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Nick is asking where the best place to spend time downtown is</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Jean couldn’t decide what she should give her husband for Christmas</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">English is spoken (by people) in many places</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">A novel will be published by that writer next year</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">All the old furniture on the sidewalk was taken away (by someone) last night</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Mike has been employed as a handyman by Mrs. Smith for the past three years</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["Adam hates certain vegetables; for example , he never eats lettuce.", "The boss always holds on to his principles no matter what happens.", "Students were lined up for the class picture according to their height.", "Unlike her (older/elder) sister, Jenny keeps complaining about everything. She seems hard to get along with.", "This is one of the areas with the busiest traffic. When (you are) crossing the street, look out for cars.", "For years, there have been many theories about what the function of the pyramids was.", "In fact, archaeologists can’t even say for sure how they were built."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Unlike her (older/elder) sister, Jenny keeps complaining about everything. She seems</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">hard to get along with</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">This is one of the areas with the busiest traffic. When (you are) crossing the street, look</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">out for cars</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">For years, there have been many theories about what the function of the pyramids was</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">In fact, archaeologists can’t even say for sure how they were built</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["When it comes to sleeping, we probably picture a nice comfortable bed.", "We imagine laying our heads on big fluffy pillows and lying under nice warm blankets.", "Most animals, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) however</strong>, sleep in very different places.", "Sea otters, for instance, sleep on their backs in the water and <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) yet</strong> don’t drown.", "When giraffes get their forty winks, they are able <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (A) to use</strong> their hips as a pillow.", "And some creatures, like the Alpine swift, can even doze off <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) while</strong> they are flying up in the sky!", "These <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (C) amazing</strong> migratory birds travel thousands of kilometers between continents every year.", "On these extremely long flights, they stay in the sky <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) for</strong> weeks or even months at a time.", "In fact, one Swiss study in 2013 showed that Alpine swifts remain in the air for even longer than we imagine.", "In this study, special sensors were attached to six birds so that their location and speed could <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) be measured</strong> at all times.", "The research team found that the swifts could cover up to 10,000 km and go as long as 200 days <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) without</strong> landing!", "Recently, some <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (D) have argued</strong> that Alpine swifts don’t actually sleep at all during these flights.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (B) In fact</strong>, they are capable of getting some shut-eye up in the sky.", "This makes them some of the coolest sleepers on earth.", "It also makes you wonder which are fluffier, pillows or clouds?"], "questions": [], "source": [null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) however</strong>  , sleep in very different places. Sea otters, for instance, sleep on their backs in the water and   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) yet</strong>   don’t drown. When giraffes get their forty winks, they are able   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (A) to use</strong>", "their hips as a pillow. And some creatures, like the Alpine swift, can even doze off   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) while</strong>", null, "These   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (C) amazing</strong>   migratory birds travel thousands of kilometers between continents every year. On these extremely long flights, they stay in the sky   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) for</strong>   weeks or even months at a time. In fact, one Swiss study in 2013 showed that Alpine swifts remain in the air for even longer than we imagine. In this study, special sensors were attached to six birds so that their location and speed could   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) be measured</strong>   at all times. The research team found that the swifts could cover up to 10,000 km and go as long as 200 days   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) without</strong>   landing!", "Recently, some   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (D) have argued</strong>   that Alpine swifts don’t actually sleep at all during these flights.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (B) In fact</strong>  , they are capable of getting some shut-eye up in the sky. This makes them some of the coolest sleepers on earth. It also makes you wonder which are fluffier, pillows or clouds?", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["Many young people do not value sleep highly enough.", "Do you know that high school students are supposed to get a(n) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) average</strong> of eight to ten hours of sleep every night?", "I always wish that I had known the power of sleep when I was a student so that I could have <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) avoided</strong> certain bad sleeping habits early on.", "I became <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (H) amazed</strong> by the importance of sleep the year after I started a new job.", "I lived a very busy life and had trouble falling asleep at night.", "I tried some ways to improve my sleep quality, and the results were really <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (J) impressive</strong>.", "The first thing I did was to stop taking a(n) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (A) nap</strong> during the day.", "I would sometimes sleep <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) from</strong> 2 p.m. to 6 p.m. on weekends, but this wasn’t really a good habit.", "It actually kept me <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (I) awake</strong> in the middle of the night.", "This made me feel <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (B) truly</strong> tired the next day and left me without any energy.", "Other things I did to help me sleep better included reducing my stress by slowing down and getting more exercise.", "I also made sure I went to bed <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (G) at</strong> the same time every night.", "All these have made a big difference in my life.", "I have become healthy and I am doing well at my job.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (F) Therefore</strong>, I now realize the importance of sleep.", "I hope you do, too!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "Many young people do not value sleep highly enough. Do you know that high school students are supposed to get a(n)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) average</strong>   of eight to ten hours of sleep every night? I always wish that I had known the power of sleep when I was a student so that I could have", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) avoided</strong>   certain bad sleeping habits early on.", "I became   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (H) amazed</strong>   by the importance of sleep the year after I started a new job. I lived a very busy life and had trouble falling asleep at night. I tried some ways to improve my sleep quality, and the results were really   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (J) impressive</strong>  . The first thing I did was to stop taking a(n) \n  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (A) nap</strong>   during the day. I would sometimes sleep   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) from</strong>   2 p.m. to 6 p.m. on weekends, but this wasn’t really a good habit. It actually kept me   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (I) awake</strong>   in the middle of the night. This made me feel   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (B) truly</strong>   tired the next day and left me without any energy.", "Other things I did to help me sleep better included reducing my stress by slowing down and getting more exercise. I also made sure I went to bed   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (G) at</strong>   the same time every night. All these have made a big difference in my life. I have become healthy and I am doing well at my job.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (F) therefore</strong>  , I now realize the importance of sleep. I hope you do, too!", null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["Have you ever wondered how you can communicate with your dog?", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) Since dogs cannot speak, we have to read their body language to better understand them</strong>.", "One way to tell what a dog is feeling is by looking at his or her sleeping behavior.", "Sometimes, your dog may sleep with his or her belly facing upward.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) Since this is a very relaxed position, scientists think this happens when a dog feels truly comfortable in his or her environment</strong>.", "You may have also seen your dog’s face or body move during sleep, or you may have heard him or her whimper or growl.", "This may happen because your dog is having a dream.", "Many scientists think that dogs can dream because they exhibit behaviors similar to humans’ when they are asleep.", "Also, their sleeping behavior can be a sign of affection toward humans.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (E) When dogs feel close to their owners, they may choose to sleep on their bed next to them or with their head on their owner’s lap</strong>.", "This behavior shows that dogs trust their owners and feel that their owners are “part of the pack.”", "Other than dogs, there are many animals that show their thoughts and feelings through their sleeping patterns.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (C) Next time you visit a zoo, be sure to look closely at sleeping primates, birds, reptiles, and sea creatures</strong>.", "You may be surprised to find that they sleep just like humans!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, "Have you ever wondered how you can communicate with your dog?   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) Since dogs cannot speak, we have to read their body language to better understand them.</strong>   One way to tell what a dog is feeling is by looking at his or her sleeping behavior. Sometimes, your dog may sleep with his or her belly facing upward.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) Since this is a very relaxed position, scientists think this happens when a dog feels truly comfortable in his or her environment.</strong>   You may have also seen your dog’s face or body move during sleep, or you may have heard him or her whimper* or growl. This may happen because your dog is having a dream. Many scientists think that dogs can dream because they exhibit behaviors similar to humans’ when they are asleep. Also, their sleeping behavior can be a sign of affection toward humans.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (E) When dogs feel close to their owners, they may choose to sleep on their bed next to them or with their head on their owner’s lap.</strong>   This behavior shows that dogs trust their owners and feel that their owners are “part of the pack.” Other than dogs, there are many animals that show their thoughts and feelings through their sleeping patterns.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (C) Next time you visit a zoo, be sure to look closely at sleeping primates, birds, reptiles, and sea creatures.</strong>   You may be surprised to find that they sleep just like humans!", null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["Most people agree that we all need to eat enough during the day to have the energy and brain power required to do everything we need to do.", "However, did you know that it is the same case with sleep?", "People need sleep because that’s what our brain needs.", "It is believed that sleep helps the brain restore its power and focus for the next day.", "If we don’t get enough sleep at night, we tend to have a hard time focusing and are a bit clumsy the next day.", "Thus, the lack of sleep over a long period of time can damage our health and even lead to death.", "Moreover, sleep also plays an important role in our ability to remember and learn.", "While we sleep at night, our brain stays active.", "It looks back on everything that happened during the day and organizes everything we have learned.", "However, during our sleep, our brain stores information more securely than when we first received it during the day.", "To do its job well, the brain needs the body to get a healthy amount of rest.", "For example, young children need 12 to 14 hours of sleep per night, and teenagers need nine hours.", "In summary, getting enough sleep is good for our health and helps us function when we’re awake.", "If you want to lead a happy life where you can be productive and maintain strong relationships with others, you should do all you can to sleep well every night!"], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ A ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the passage mainly about?", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(A) Why sleep is important to us.</strong>", "(B) How we can get a good night’s sleep.", "(C) When we have more energy and brain power.", "(D) What we should do to improve our memory and learning capacity.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ D ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following is NOT mentioned in the passage?", "(A) Teenagers need nine hours of sleep every night.", "(B) Lack of sleep for too long a period may cause death.", "(C) Eating well keeps us energetic and keeps our brain active.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) Getting enough sleep enables us to become masters in many fields.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t3.\tWhere is this passage most likely to appear?", "(A) A novel.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) A science magazine.</strong>", "(C) A history textbook.", "(D) A travel book."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["How Do Animals Survive the Winter?", "When winter arrives, animals find various ways to survive in the chilly weather.", "The following are some examples of how wild creatures adapt to cold conditions.", "1. Many animals—such as bears, bats, and groundhogs—hibernate to save their energy.", "2. Some birds, like storks and swallows, fly to warmer places or grow thicker feathers to stay warm.", "3. Some animals survive the winter without hibernating. For example, beavers and squirrels store a lot of food for the whole winter, while shrews change what they eat in the winter.", "4. Many insects find a dry place to spend the winter. For instance, a moth spends the winter in a cocoon. Spiders, on the other hand, have a special kind of blood that keeps them from freezing.", "5. Snakes and frogs burrow into mud at the bottom of ponds and lakes. Throughout winter, their skin absorbs oxygen from the water as they sleep, and the mud keeps them warm.", "6. Captive or zoo animals often do not hibernate. It’s easier for them to survive in winter."], "questions": ["For the purpose of (1)  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">surviving</strong>   cold winters, wild animals develop a \n(2)    <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">variety</strong>    of useful habits, such as hibernating and storing food, to help them stay alive in the chilly weather.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that especially change their living environments for the winter.       <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">B D E</strong>", "(A) Bats.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) Storks.</strong>", "(C) Beavers.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) Moths.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(E) Snakes.</strong>", "(F) Captive animals.", "3.\tWhich word in the passage means “takes in something gradually”?\n    <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">absorbs</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "L04": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["Our teacher gave us cookies as a reward for doing well on the exam.", "I am surprised to learn that Emma has the ability to speak six languages.", "If you detect thick smoke in your house, you should call the fire department at once.", "Research has shown that smoking can increase one’s risk of developing heart disease.", "I plan to accomplish a lot of tasks today, so I am trying to focus on what I am doing now and not to get distracted.", "If teachers wish to manage their classes effectively on the first day of school, they had better lay down some ground rules.", "Since both of their parents died in the accident, it is hard to predict what will become of the kids.", "It is reported that an Arizona woman was pricked by an HIV-infected needle and later died of AIDS.", "I go to the supermarket very often, but usually I don’t have anything specific to buy.", "I just like to look around.", "To catch Julie’s attention, Mike dressed up and even asked for a chance to perform magic at the party."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["Our assignment today is to read twenty pages in our science textbook.", "It takes creativity to keep coming up with interesting new ideas.", "I like the apartment a lot because the rent is not high and the location is perfect.", "Studies have shown that exposure to too much solar radiation will cause skin cancer.", "Mother said that she wouldn’t allow us to watch TV if we couldn’t behave ourselves."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["We should be thankful to anyone who/that helps us out in times of trouble.", "I have read the term paper which/that was written by David and John.", "Do you know the man with whom our English teacher is talking/(who(m)/that) our English teacher is talking with?", "Look, there are an old man and his dog that are crossing the busy street.", "I attended the Christmas party which/that was held by my friend Jenny.", "Leo’s mother, who lives in Thailand, has five grandchildren.", "James felt sad about the loss of his best friend, whom he would never meet again.", "Starbucks, which was first opened in Seattle, Washington, is a chain coffee shop.", "Tonight I have to brush up on biology, which is the most difficult subject for me."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">We should be thankful to anyone who/that helps us out in times of trouble</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I have read the term paper which/that was written by David and John</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Do you know the man with whom our English teacher is talking/</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(who(m)/that) our English teacher is talking with</strong>?", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Look, there are an old man and his dog that are crossing the busy street</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I attended the Christmas party which/that was held by my friend Jenny</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Leo’s mother, who lives in Thailand, has five grandchildren</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">James felt sad about the loss of his best friend, whom he would never meet again</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Starbucks, which was first opened in Seattle, Washington, is a chain coffee shop</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Tonight I have to brush up on biology, which is the most difficult subject for me</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["I’m very happy to come across you. I want to ask you about tomorrow’s math test.", "When the earthquake struck, the lights went out all of a sudden , and the town was left in darkness.", "Before buying the farm, he carried out a land survey to work out how much it was really worth.", "Due to extreme climate changes, many kinds of animals have disappeared from the earth.", "Alison thought she could handle the job, but it turned out to be too difficult for her.", "The following are a few tips which/that may help you solve your problems.", "Or you can turn to Mr. Smith, who is an expert in this field."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Due to extreme climate changes, many kinds of animals have disappeared from the earth</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Alison thought she could handle the job, but it turned out to be too difficult for her</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The following are a few tips which/that may help you solve your problems</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Or you can turn to Mr. Smith, who is an expert in this field</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["Tessa was walking down the street one day.", "Along her way, she saw a beautiful Labrador <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) which</strong> was sitting outside the bakery.", "She stopped, smiled at the friendly-looking dog, and took a close look at it.", "Its big ears looked so much softer than a human’s, and its kind eyes seemed to be <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) inviting</strong> her to come closer.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) For this reason</strong>, she approached the dog.", "However, when she was just about to pat the dog’s golden head, the owner of the bakery opened the door and stopped her <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) by</strong> making a friendly gesture.", "“That’s a specially <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) trained</strong> service dog, young lady.", "Please don’t touch it.”", "Tessa was quite surprised to be stopped <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) in this way</strong>.", "She withdrew her hand and looked a little embarrassed and confused.", "The owner saw <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) that</strong> she didn’t quite understand.", "Therefore, he added, “This is an <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (D) amazing</strong> guide dog for a blind customer of mine.", "It’s trained to do certain kinds of tasks.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) Since</strong> the dog might get distracted if a stranger pets it, we should not interrupt it.", "If the dog pays attention to other humans and doesn’t perform its job properly, it could mean trouble, or even danger, for the blind person.", "Therefore, you should never hand a working dog a snack or treat, either.”", "Tessa nodded and smiled, no longer having a <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (A) sense</strong> of embarrassment.", "Better yet, she had learned a lesson."], "questions": [], "source": ["Tessa was walking down the street one day. Along her way, she saw a beautiful Labrador   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) which</strong>   was sitting outside the bakery. She stopped, smiled at the friendly-looking \ndog, and took a close look at it. Its big ears looked so much softer than a human’s, and its kind eyes seemed to be   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) inviting</strong>   her to come closer.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) For this reason</strong>  , she approached the dog. However, when she was just about to pat the dog’s golden head, the owner of the bakery opened the door and stopped her   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) by</strong>   making a friendly gesture.", "“That’s a specially   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) trained</strong>   service dog, young lady. Please don’t touch it.”", "Tessa was quite surprised to be stopped   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) in this way</strong>  . She withdrew her hand and looked a little embarrassed and confused.", "The owner saw   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) that</strong>   she didn’t quite understand. Therefore, he added, “This is an", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (D) amazing</strong>   guide dog for a blind customer of mine. It’s trained to do certain kinds of tasks.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) Since</strong>   the dog might get distracted* if a stranger pets it, we should not interrupt* it. If the dog pays attention to other humans and doesn’t perform its job properly, it could mean trouble, or even danger, for the blind person. Therefore, you should never hand a working dog a snack or treat, either.”", "Tessa nodded and smiled, no longer having a   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (A) sense</strong>   of embarrassment. Better yet, she had learned a lesson.", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["Have you ever heard the term “K-9”?", "Police dogs are called K-9s <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) due to</strong> the word “canine,” which means “dog” or “related to dogs.”", "Because of their extremely sharp sense of smell, dogs <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) perform</strong> very well in tracking tasks.", "Thus, they can be <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (I) trained</strong> to help police find illegal items, like drugs.", "It’s also been proven that dogs are <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (H) far</strong> smarter than many other animals.", "In addition, their <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (J) ability</strong> to remember certain commands and their loyalty make them highly valuable members of the police force.", "In fact, officers could hardly <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (A) manage</strong> to maintain law and order without them!", "Among K-9s, the German Shepherd and the Belgian Malinois are the breeds which are most commonly <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (D) assigned</strong> police duties.", "Their “jobs” include searching and digging, sniffing things <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (G) out</strong>, chasing and holding suspects, and protecting police officers, to name just a few.", "Different breeds tend to be skilled in different tasks, but any good police dog should be smart and brave.", "They should also, of course, have a(n) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) keen</strong> sense of smell.", "Whatever they do, K-9s usually work very hard.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (F) Therefore</strong>, remember to always show respect and never touch a police dog that’s on duty.", "After all, we wouldn’t want to throw these top dogs off the scent!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "Have you ever heard the term “K-9”? Police dogs are called K-9s   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) due to</strong>   the word “canine,” which means “dog” or “related to dogs.” Because of their extremely sharp sense of smell, dogs   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) perform</strong>   very well in tracking tasks. Thus, they can be   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (I) trained</strong>   to help police find illegal items, like drugs. It’s also been proven that dogs are   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (H) far</strong>   smarter than many other animals. In addition, their   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (J) ability</strong>   to remember certain commands and their loyalty make them highly valuable members of the police force. In fact, officers could hardly   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (A) manage</strong>   to maintain law and order without them!", "Among K-9s, the German Shepherd and the Belgian Malinois are the breeds* which are most commonly   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (D) assigned</strong>   police duties. Their “jobs” include searching and digging, sniffing things   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (G) out</strong>  , chasing and holding suspects, and protecting police officers, to name just a few. Different breeds tend to be skilled in different tasks, but any good police dog should be smart and brave. They should also, of course, have a(n)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) keen</strong>   sense of smell. Whatever they do, K-9s usually work very hard.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (F) therefore</strong>  , remember to always show respect and never touch a police dog that’s on duty. After all, we wouldn’t want to throw these top dogs off the scent!", null, null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["Dogs are known as “man’s best friend,” but did you know that birds have also worked together with humans for thousands of years?", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) Falconry, or hawking, is the art of hunting together with a bird of prey</strong>.", "This practice dates back to ancient times, when birds of prey helped humans survive extreme climates by hunting smaller animals—such as foxes, squirrels, rabbits, and fish—for them.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (B) Today, hunters in Mongolia and America still use birds to catch their prey</strong>.", "Red-tailed hawks and golden eagles are two of the most popular bird choices they work with.", "This is mainly because of these birds’ extraordinary eyesight, which is many times sharper than a human’s.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) Scientific studies have even revealed that these birds can see colors that humans cannot</strong>.", "This is why they can find animals hidden among trees and rocks.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) It is believed that eagles and hawks can even spot a worm crawling on the ground from atop a tall building or a rabbit that is two miles away</strong>.", "The excellent vision of these two birds of prey makes them perfect hunting partners."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, "Dogs are known as “man’s best friend,” but did you know that birds have also worked together with humans for thousands of years?   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) Falconry, or hawking, is the art of hunting together with a bird of prey.</strong>   This practice dates back to ancient times, when birds of prey helped humans survive extreme climates by hunting smaller animals—such as foxes, squirrels, rabbits, and fish—for them.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (B) Today, hunters in Mongolia and America still use birds to catch their prey.</strong>   Red-tailed hawks and golden eagles are two of the most popular bird choices they work with. This is mainly because of these birds’ extraordinary* eyesight, which is many times sharper than a human’s.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) Scientific studies have even revealed that these birds can see colors that humans cannot.</strong>   This is why they can find animals hidden among trees and rocks.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) It is believed that eagles and hawks can even spot a worm crawling on the ground from atop a tall building or a rabbit that is two miles away.</strong>   \nThe excellent vision of these two birds of prey makes them perfect hunting partners.", null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["Service dogs are often very cute and well-behaved.", "This is why people who are scared of dogs might think it is safe to pet them.", "However, a service dog is always on duty, and the job it is doing—protecting its owner’s life—is very important.", "So, what should you do when you see a service dog?", "The most important thing is not to pet it.", "Doing so is not only impolite but also dangerous because you may distract the dog from the important job it is doing.", "In fact, you should not try to interact with the dog at all.", "This means you should not look at it, try to distract it, get too close to it, or touch its equipment.", "Remember, though service dogs may be cute, it’s best to keep your hands off!"], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the best title for this passage?", "(A) Why We Should Keep Service Dogs", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) How We Should Treat Service Dogs</strong>", "(C)\tWhere We Can Find Good Service Dogs", "(D) What Benefits We Can Get from Service Dogs", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following statements is true about service dogs?", "(A) They are dangerous to pet.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) They are valuable to their owners.</strong>", "(C) They are not likely to be distracted.", "(D) They are faithful to everyone around them.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t3.\tWhat advice does the author offer to people who come across a service dog?", "(A) Go pet it.", "(B) Try to interact with it.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) Keep a distance from it.</strong>", "(D) Get close enough to touch its equipment."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["R&amp;B, funk, and hip hop are three popular types of music that are connected in many ways.", "However, despite their similarities, each has unique traits that differentiate one from the others.", "R&amp;B singers use special vocal techniques to sing elegantly.", "Their lyrics often include references to love, heartbreak, and even politics.", "Some R&amp;B songs are sad, while others are full of hope and happiness.", "The melodies are usually slow and smooth.", "While the main focus of R&amp;B is the singer, the singing and instrumentation play equally important roles in funk.", "This type of music focuses on upbeat guitar and bass lines.", "Therefore, these two musical instruments often play solos in funk arrangements.", "Additionally, the themes of funk music cover a wide range of topics, including partying, social commentary, love, and life situations.", "Though influenced by R&amp;B and funk, hip hop is quite different.", "In contrast to funk, its focus is less on the music, and it generally lacks singing, unlike R&amp;B.", "Instead, hip hop comes with a beat and usually some simple instrumentation, and a rapper speaks rhythmically over them instead of singing.", "The lyrics of hip hop may cover partying, drugs, social events, and life situations."], "questions": ["The (1) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">differences</strong>   between R&amp;B, funk, and hip hop show that each has its unique features, which make these three types of music highly accepted and raise their (2)  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">popularity</strong>   with their audiences.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are true for the three types of music. \n     <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">A C E</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(A) R&amp;B is known for its elegant and smooth melodies.</strong>", "(B) Funk focuses on speaking and the use of guitars.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) R&amp;B and funk contain more topics about romance than hip hop.</strong>", "(D) Unlike R&amp;B, hip hop doesn’t require any vocal techniques from singers.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(E) Instrumentation is important in both hip hop and funk.</strong>", "(F) R&amp;B, funk, and hip hop cover topics of partying, society, and politics.", "3.\tWhat does the word “others” in the second paragraph refer to? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">other R&amp;B songs</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "L05": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["I’d like to have a talk with you at your convenience.", "When’s the best time?", "It is believed that a happy family provides a loving environment in which children feel safe and secure.", "That homeless man is poor and doesn’t have a suitcase for his belongings, so he carries them in a plastic bag.", "If you consume enough fruit and vegetables, you’ll become healthier.", "The police have taken the unknown substance to the lab so that scientists there can determine what it is.", "Stephanie made her way across the crowded room to where her friend was standing.", "This company plans to invest a huge amount of money in the production of computer products.", "Poisonous materials should always be kept in a locked cabinet, so that children can’t touch them.", "Obviously Helen’s boss didn’t like her ideas, for he walked out of the meeting room after only a few minutes.", "It is useless to envy other people for their success and good fortune.", "Instead, you should make more of an effort to succeed."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["Fewer trees will be cut down if we recycle more paper.", "Steve wondered whether it would be proper to knock at Ann’s door late at night.", "After the job interview, Joe was eager to know if he would be hired as an engineer.", "This river contains a high level of harmful chemicals.", "You’ll get sick if you drink the water.", "When you live in a foreign country, you have to spend a lot of time getting used to your new surroundings."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["Our teacher made us read a whole lesson in half an hour.", "Michael had his daughter drive him to the airport to meet his old friend.", "Susan’s parents don’t let her stay out too late at night.", "My mother has me practice ballet after school every day.", "Robert didn’t go to school yesterday because he was seriously injured.", "The mayor has announced that there will be no school tomorrow because of a powerful typhoon.", "Linda has lost a lot of weight because she has eaten less junk food recently.", "Julia and Jeff broke up because they valued different things in life.", "Many people choose to live in the suburbs because of high housing prices in downtown areas."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "Our teacher <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">made us read a whole lesson in half an hour</strong>.", null, "Michael <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">had his daughter drive him to the airport to meet his old friend</strong>.", null, "Susan’s parents <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">don’t let her stay out too late at night</strong>.", null, "My mother <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">has me practice ballet after school every day</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Robert didn’t go to school yesterday because he was seriously injured</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The mayor has announced that there will be no school tomorrow because of a</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">powerful typhoon</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Linda has lost a lot of weight because she has eaten less junk food recently</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Julia and Jeff broke up because they valued different things in life</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Many people choose to live in the suburbs because of high housing prices in</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">downtown areas</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["The woman warned her son that he would end up in prison if he continued to steal.", "In this high-tech world, we’ve almost forgotten how we searched for information in the past before the Internet came along .", "I can’t carry these heavy boxes on my own . Would you please help me?", "More and more people are (getting) tired of living in the city and (are) thinking of moving (out) to the country one day.", "As/Because Jeff got to the party too early, he had to wait there alone for a while until the others arrived.", "Because of your timely help, I could finish my math homework.", "To express my thanks, let me take you to a movie and then treat you to dinner."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">More and more people are (getting) tired of living in the city and (are) thinking of\t\nmoving (out) to the country one day</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">As/Because Jeff got to the party too early, he had to wait there alone for a while until \t\nthe others arrived</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Because of your timely help, I could finish my math homework</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">To express my thanks, let me take you to a movie and then treat you to dinner</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["Do you throw your food waste in the garbage?", "You’d better not <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) because of</strong> its great environmental cost.", "Instead, you should think about composting.", "Composting is much easier than you may think.", "If you have space outside your home, just create a pile of dirt and throw your food waste onto it.", "However, if your property is smaller and your compost would have to be right <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) next to</strong> your home, use a closed bin instead.", "Even if you live in an apartment, you don’t have to worry!", "You can buy special warm compost bins that can stay inside your home.", "Most people believe <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) that</strong> such bins must smell awful, but the best part is that they’re not that smelly!", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) According to</strong> experts, there are some tricks to composting.", "The first tip is to compost as much brown material (e.g., dead leaves, grains, wood) as green material (e.g., vegetable scraps, fruit peels, grass).", "If you follow this rule, you <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) are going to</strong> get high-quality soil.", "Also, if your pile is very big, you’ll need to mix it from time to time <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) to keep</strong> the oxygen flowing through it.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (A) Finally</strong>, remember that meat and dairy products can’t be composted.", "They’ll <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) make</strong> your pile smelly and will attract animals.", "If you follow these tips, you will have dark, rich soil that’ll be great for growing plants <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) sooner</strong> than you think.", "You can spread this soil in your garden or add it to your potted plants.", "If you don’t choose either of these options, you can share it with someone <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (B) who</strong> does.", "Composting is a practice that can really improve our environment.", "You should definitely consider giving it a try."], "questions": [], "source": ["Do you throw your food waste in the garbage? You’d better not   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) because of</strong>   its great environmental cost. Instead, you should think about composting*. Composting is much easier than you may think. If you have space outside your home, just create a pile of dirt and throw your food waste onto it. However, if your property is smaller and your compost would have to be right   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) next to</strong>   your home, use a closed bin instead. Even if you live in an apartment, you don’t have to worry! You can buy special warm compost bins that can stay inside your home. Most people believe that such bins must smell awful, but the best part is that they’re not   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) that</strong>   smelly!", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) According to</strong>   experts, there are some tricks to composting. The first tip is to compost as much brown material (e.g., dead leaves, grains, wood) as green material (e.g., vegetable scraps, fruit peels, grass). If you follow this rule, you   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) are going to</strong>   get high-quality soil. Also, if your pile is very big, you’ll need to mix it from time to time   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) to keep</strong>   the oxygen flowing through it.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (A) Finally</strong>  , remember that meat and dairy products can’t be composted. They’ll", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) make</strong>   your pile smelly and will attract animals.", "If you follow these tips, you will have dark, rich soil that’ll be great for growing plants   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) sooner</strong>   than you think. You can spread this soil in your garden or add it to your potted plants. If you don’t choose either of these options, you can share it with someone", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (B) who</strong>   does.", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["I’ve always been told that it is everyone’s responsibility to help care for the Earth.", "In other words, each of us should make efforts to protect the <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) environment</strong>.", "However, despite this idea, most of us are still <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) causing</strong> environmental damage day in and day out.", "This is why, one could argue, we’re constantly surrounded <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (H) by</strong> strange diseases and the frightening effects of climate change.", "Such ills are <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (J) obviously</strong> harming humans, and some even suggest that it’s Mother Nature’s way of striking back!", "Aren’t you tired <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (A) of</strong> harming our precious Earth?", "Isn’t it time for change?", "We can’t save the Earth <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (F) on our own</strong>, but we can all start small and think about how our daily actions affect the planet.", "We can also start to live by the 3 Rs: reduce, reuse, and <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (I) recycle</strong>.", "To reduce, for example, we can buy only what we’ll definitely <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (B) consume</strong> instead of creating waste.", "Also, we can avoid buying and using single-use <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (D) products</strong> by reusing more.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (G) Lastly</strong>, we can buy products that are made with eco-friendly materials, like paper that can easily be recycled.", "Let’s come up with more “go green” goals and see how many we can actually achieve by Earth Day!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "I’ve always been told that it is everyone’s responsibility to help care for the Earth. In other words, each of us should make efforts to protect the   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) environment</strong>  . However, despite this idea, most of us are still   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) causing</strong>   environmental damage day in and day out. This is why, one could argue, we’re constantly surrounded   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (H) by</strong>   strange diseases and the frightening effects of climate change. Such ills are   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (J) obviously</strong>   harming humans, and some even suggest that it’s Mother Nature’s way of striking back!", "Aren’t you tired   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (A) of</strong>   harming our precious Earth? Isn’t it time for change? We can’t save the Earth   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (F) on our own</strong>  , but we can all start small and think about how our daily actions affect the planet. We can also start to live by the 3 Rs: reduce, reuse, and   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (I) recycle</strong>  . To reduce, for example, we can buy only what we’ll definitely   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (B) consume</strong>   instead of creating waste. Also, we can avoid buying and using single-use   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (D) products</strong>   by reusing more.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (G) lastly</strong>  , we can buy products that are made with eco-friendly materials, like paper that can easily be recycled.", null, null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["I am a stack of paper that has been sitting in an office for months now.", "The office lady, Jane, is my only companion.", "She sits near me, and we interact every day.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) I like to think that Jane is my friend, but I’m not sure if she thinks so</strong>.", "I am saying this because I don’t think Jane is really aware of my feelings.", "Sometimes she can even be cruel to me.", "She often writes on me and even throws parts of me into the trash can!", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) This sad and sometimes painful office life makes me miss my past a lot</strong>.", "Before becoming a stack of paper, I was a handsome pine tree, standing tall and proud at the edge of a mighty mountain.", "Back then, I always had plenty of pine tree friends to talk to.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) But then, one day, a group of humans came along and started hurting us with axes and machines</strong>.", "That was a terrible day.", "Even now, I can still remember the painful cries of my fellow trees and the panicked animals that were being left homeless and hungry as the humans took us away.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) I heard the humans saying they were going to use us to make paper and build houses where people could live</strong>.", "If only they knew how many other lives they had ruined by taking us away!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, "I am a stack of paper that has been sitting in an office for months now. The office lady, Jane, is my only companion*. She sits near me, and we interact* every day.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) I like to think that Jane is my friend, but I’m not sure if she thinks so.</strong>    I am saying this because I don’t think Jane is really aware of my feelings. Sometimes she can even be cruel to me. She often writes on me and even throws parts of me into the trash can!", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) This sad and sometimes painful office life makes me miss my past a lot.</strong>   Before becoming a stack of paper, I was a handsome pine tree, standing tall and proud at the edge of a mighty mountain. Back then, I always had plenty of pine tree friends to talk to.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) But then, one day, a group of humans came along and started hurting us with axes and machines.</strong>   That was a terrible day. Even now, I can still remember the painful cries of my fellow trees and the panicked animals that were being left homeless and hungry as the humans took us away.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) I heard the humans saying they were going to use us to make paper and build houses where people could live.</strong>   If only they knew how many other lives they had ruined by taking us away!", null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["Plastic straws are not good for the Earth.", "They take many years to break down into smaller pieces.", "Moreover, they are single-use items that are often used quickly and then thrown away, just like garbage bags, plastic cups, and takeout boxes.", "Such items make up a large amount of garbage that is increasing at an alarming rate.", "For example, single-use plastic straws are creating a big problem in our world today.", "They can’t be recycled because they are too light.", "This means these straws do not get separated from other garbage at recycling dumps.", "Even worse, they begin to fill up these dumps.", "As plastic straws gradually break down, they separate into very small plastic pieces called microplastics.", "These microplastics can be eaten by birds and sea animals accidentally.", "After being eaten by these creatures, they stay in their stomachs and can even kill them.", "Then, when we humans eat those animals, we also eat the microplastics, and this can damage our health.", "The best way to fix this problem is to stop using single-use plastic straws.", "Next time you buy a drink, don’t ask for a straw, or you can use your own reusable straw.", "Such small steps can make a big difference in saving our world, so let’s say no to plastic straws!"], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the passage mainly about?", "(A) The types of single-use items.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) The problem caused by plastic straws.</strong>", "(C) The best way to deal with plastic products.", "(D) The damage microplastics are causing to the environment.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ D ）</strong>\t2.\tAccording to the passage, which of the following statements about plastic straws is NOT true?", "(A) They can’t be recycled.", "(B) They fill up recycling dumps.", "(C) They can cause animals to die.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) They don’t break down into smaller pieces.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ A ）</strong>\t3.\tHow does the author conclude the passage?", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(A) By offering a solution.</strong>", "(B) By asking further questions.", "(C) By predicting future problems.", "(D) By summarizing the ideas in the passage."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["The issue of waste has become more and more important when it comes to protecting our environment.", "That’s why Henry’s group chose waste as the topic of their project this time.", "Read the following discussion between the members of Henry’s group.", "I think it’s important that in our project we learn how various types of waste are disposed of and how they influence our lives.", "Please share any information you collect on the topic with us.", "Based on my research, there are three main types of waste: general waste, recyclable waste, and organic waste.", "Of these, organic waste could be the most environmentally friendly.", "That’s correct.", "Organic waste, such as food waste, or leftovers, can be broken down into compost, which can then be used to grow plants.", "It’s important to remember that recycling allows us to reuse valuable resources and reduce unnecessary waste.", "However, we should note that different places have different policies about the collection of recyclable materials.", "Do you know that we can generate electricity from organic waste after microbes break it down into gas?", "It’s quite amazing, isn’t it?", "I also believe it’s important to list the ways to dispose of special items that contain materials harmful to the environment, such as batteries.", "This way, people can learn how to protect our environment."], "questions": ["For the (1)  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">protection</strong>   of the environment, Henry and the other members of his group collected information and (2)  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">discussed</strong>   the issue of waste in terms of its disposal and influences.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) in the above discussion, which ONES talk about waste that can become reusable resources?     <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">B C D E</strong>", "3.\tWhat does the word “it” in Annie’s message refer to? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">organic waste</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "L06": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["White stands for purity in Western countries, but it represents death in China.", "As children mature, they often try to gain more independence from their parents.", "Before medicine was invented, ancient people cured themselves with herbs, such as garlic and ginger.", "We’ll have a big family celebration next Friday night for my father’s 70th birthday.", "This monument in the city square was built in memory of our country’s heroes.", "Some people dislike zoos and argue that wild animals should have more freedom.", "Many tourists visit Hawaii every year to enjoy the beaches and beautiful scenery.", "Before you enter the house, please wipe your feet on the mat to remove any dirt from your shoes.", "The wax statue at the museum looks so real that it seems as if the actual person were standing there in front of you.", "The Eiffel Tower was built in 1889.", "Now, it is a famous landmark in Paris."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["What really attracted Trudy to the job was the paid vacations.", "The problem of global warming is getting worse, and it may threaten our living environment.", "I cherish the card Jenny gave to me because it is symbolic of our friendship.", "Some slaves in the American South were treated well by their masters, but they were still not free people.", "Eric’s doctor suggested that he sleep on a firm mattress to benefit his back."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["The question is so complicated that no one can really answer it.", "It is such a good opportunity that you shouldn’t miss it.", "The magician performed so poorly that his audience soon got bored.", "The Chens were such nice neighbors that we were sad when they moved.", "It is the high price of the car that keeps Jeff from buying it.", "It was due to Randy’s carelessness that he was fired.", "It was the car accident that finally made Peter realize the importance of safe driving.", "It was while I was taking a shower that my best friend Ethan called.", "It was because Kevin skipped too many classes that he didn’t pass the course."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The question is so complicated that no one can really answer it</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is such a good opportunity that you shouldn’t miss it</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The magician performed so poorly that his audience soon got bored</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The Chens were such nice neighbors that we were sad when they moved</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is the high price of the car that keeps Jeff from buying it</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was due to Randy’s carelessness that he was fired</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was the car accident that finally made Peter realize the importance of safe</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">driving</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was while I was taking a shower that my best friend Ethan called</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was because Kevin skipped too many classes that he didn’t pass the course</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["Even though Max had tried to get rid of the stain on his shirt, a mark was still visible.", "It is sad to learn that four out of the world’s six species of great apes are close to extinction.", "Last weekend, Sarah paid a visit to her grandmother’s house to help plant flowers in the garden.", "Mr. Wang is not just a famous pop singer but one of the richest men in the country.", "According to studies, if children are exposed to violent video games for a long time, they may develop violent behavior.", "Mr. Davis was so generous that he presented the school with a check which could cover all the costs of the new library.", "It was through this act that he wanted to share his message of kindness with all people."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Mr. Wang is not just a famous pop singer but one of the richest men in the country</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">According to studies, if children are exposed to violent video games for a long time, \t\nthey may develop violent behavior</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Mr. Davis was so generous that he presented the school with a check which could cover</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">all the costs of the new library</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was through this act that he wanted to share his message of kindness with all</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">people</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["Just as the Statue of Liberty is recognized as a symbol of freedom, so is Eugène Delacroix’s painting Liberty Leading the People, a representation of liberty.", "Liberty Leading the People has three features in common with the Statue of Liberty.", "First, it was also created by a Frenchman.", "Second, it was also created <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) to celebrate</strong> freedom.", "Finally, it also includes a tribute to Libertas, the Roman goddess of liberty.", "Liberty Lead<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) in</strong>g the People was painted in the Romantic style in 1830.", "Its subject is the July Revolution, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) which</strong> was a significant event in France’s history.", "The painting was purchased by the French government in 1831 and has been hanging in the Louvre Museum since 1874.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) Over time</strong>, Delacroix’s painting has become one of the most famous symbols of the July Revolution and the French love of freedom.", "Delacroix’s painting shows ordinary French citizens who are charging and <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) firing</strong> their guns at the soldiers of King Charles X.", "In front of these brave people is the figure of a fearless female freedom fighter.", "Her dress is torn, so her bare breasts <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) are exposed to</strong> the enemy.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (A) In</strong> her left hand is a gun, and in her right is the future French flag.", "This is Libertas, the goddess of liberty.", "She is leading the French citizens in their fight for freedom in the July Revolution.", "The <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (B) full</strong> duration of this revolution was but 72 hours.", "By the <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) end</strong> of these “Three Glorious Days,” the fighters had taken back their precious freedom from the king.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (C) Since</strong> the unjust and greedy king had lost his crown, the people of France no longer had to suffer under his cruel rule.", "Liberty had led them to a better, freer future."], "questions": [], "source": ["Just as the Statue of Liberty is recognized as a symbol of freedom, so is Eugène Delacroix’s painting Liberty Leading the People, a representation of liberty. Liberty Leading the People has three features in common with the Statue of Liberty. First, it was also created by a Frenchman. Second, it was also created   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) to celebrate</strong>   freedom. Finally, it also includes a tribute* to Libertas, the Roman goddess of liberty.", "Liberty Leading the People was painted   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) in</strong>   the Romantic style in 1830. Its subject is the July Revolution*,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (C) which</strong>   was a significant event in France’s history. The painting was purchased by the French government in 1831 and has been hanging in the Louvre Museum since 1874.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) Over time</strong>  , Delacroix’s painting has become one of the most famous symbols of the July Revolution and the French love of freedom.", "Delacroix’s painting shows ordinary French citizens who are charging and   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) firing</strong>   \ntheir guns at the soldiers of King Charles X. In front of these brave people is the figure of a fearless female freedom fighter. Her dress is torn, so her bare breasts   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) are exposed to</strong>   the enemy.\n  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (A) In</strong>   her left hand is a gun, and in her right is the future French flag. This is Libertas, the goddess of liberty. She is leading the French citizens in their fight for freedom in the July Revolution.", "The   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (B) full</strong>   duration* of this revolution was but 72 hours. By the   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) end</strong>   of these “Three Glorious* Days,” the fighters had taken back their precious freedom from the king.\n  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (C) Since</strong>   the unjust and greedy king had lost his crown, the people of France no longer had to suffer under his cruel rule. Liberty had led them to a better, freer future.", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["Abraham Lincoln became the 16th president of the United States in 1861.", "At that time, the North and the South had been fighting for over a hundred years over the issue of <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) slavery</strong>.", "With the task of resolving this difficult problem laid <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) at</strong> his feet, Lincoln’s main goal as president was to once more unite the country.", "At a time when the Civil War was raging, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (F) however</strong>, this did not seem possible until Lincoln’s Gettysburg Address in 1863.", "That was also the year Lincoln approved a change to the law to effectively put an end to slavery.", "According to historians, Lincoln had always seen slavery as <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) unfair</strong>.", "However, it took him a long time to figure out what to do about the wrongful <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (E) treatment</strong> of African Americans.", "Shockingly, just as people were <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (G) celebrating</strong> the end of the Civil War and Lincoln’s re-election in 1865, he was killed.", "He was shot <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (H) in</strong> Washington, D.C., while watching a play with his wife.", "Without doubt, Lincoln was certainly a key figure in bringing <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (J) freedom</strong> to African Americans all across the country.", "He will thus always be remembered as one of the most <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) symbolic</strong> presidents of all time.", "His great leadership and stories continue to be a great influence across America and <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (I) around</strong> the world.", "His memory lives on!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "Abraham Lincoln became the 16th president of the United States in 1861. At that time, the North and the South had been fighting for over a hundred years over the issue of   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) slavery</strong>  . \nWith the task of resolving this difficult problem laid   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) at</strong>   his feet, Lincoln’s main goal as president was to once more unite the country. At a time when the Civil War was raging,", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (F) however</strong>  , this did not seem possible until Lincoln’s Gettysburg Address* in 1863. That was also the year Lincoln approved a change to the law to effectively put an end to slavery.", "According to historians, Lincoln had always seen slavery as   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) unfair</strong>  . However, it took him a long time to figure out what to do about the wrongful   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (E) treatment</strong>   of African Americans. Shockingly, just as people were   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (G) celebrating</strong>   the end of the Civil War and Lincoln’s re-election in 1865, he was killed. He was shot   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (H) in</strong>   Washington, D.C., while watching a play with his wife.", "Without doubt, Lincoln was certainly a key figure in bringing   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (J) freedom</strong>   to African Americans all across the country. He will thus always be remembered as one of the most", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) symbolic</strong>   presidents of all time. His great leadership and stories continue to be a great influence across America and   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (I) around</strong>   the world. His memory lives on!", null, null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["In the heart of Taipei City’s Zhongzheng District stands an important monument and major tourist attraction that was originally constructed in 1980 to honor Taiwan’s late president Chiang Kai-shek.", "Its name is the National Chiang Kai-shek Memorial Hall.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) The memorial hall is surrounded by a park that contains two other important structures</strong>.", "In the northwest corner of the park stands the National Concert Hall, while in the southwest corner is the National Theater.", "As for the memorial hall itself, it takes up the entire eastern side of the park.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (B) This hall’s construction includes several features of special importance</strong>.", "For example, the hall’s roof has eight sides, a number that often symbolizes good fortune and wealth in Chinese culture.", "Additionally, there are eighty-nine steps leading up to the central room of the hall to represent Chiang Kai-shek’s age when he died.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (E) Moreover, the white and blue colors of the hall stand for the blue sky and white sun on the Republic of China’s flag</strong>.", "Finally, in the middle of the park lies “Freedom Square,” which is a public space for everyone to enjoy.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) The name is a reference to Taiwan’s thriving democracy, and it is certainly a space for the people</strong>.", "Students, athletes, and soldiers often go there to practice for various performances.", "Moreover, the annual Lantern Festival celebrations are often held there."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) The memorial hall is surrounded by a park that contains two other important structures.</strong>   In the northwest corner of the park stands the National Concert Hall, while in the southwest corner is the National Theater. As for the memorial hall itself, it takes up the entire eastern side of the park.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (B) This hall’s construction includes several features of special importance.</strong>   For example, the hall’s roof has eight sides, a number that often symbolizes good fortune and wealth in Chinese culture. Additionally, there are eighty-nine steps leading up to the central room of the hall to represent Chiang Kai-shek’s age when he died. \n  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (E) Moreover, the white and blue colors of the hall stand for the blue sky and white sun on the Republic of China’s flag.</strong>", "Finally, in the middle of the park lies “Freedom Square,” which is a public space for everyone to enjoy.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) The name is a reference to Taiwan’s thriving democracy, and it is certainly a space for the people.</strong>   Students, athletes, and soldiers often go there to practice for various performances. Moreover, the annual* Lantern Festival celebrations are often held there.", null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["The word “memorial” comes from the Latin word for “memory.”", "Memorials can be found all over the world.", "Most of them were originally built to honor someone or something, but this isn’t always the case.", "In fact, they can serve many different functions.", "The following are some world-famous memorials, each of which serves a specific function.", "First, the Taj Mahal in Agra, India, is a beautiful site built with white marble and decorated with precious jewels.", "For many tourists today, it is a must-visit in one’s lifetime.", "However, originally, it was built by Indian emperor Shah Jahan for his favorite wife, Mumtaz Mahal, and is meant to be a symbol of everlasting love.", "Another equally famous tourist attraction is the Great Wall of China, which was built to keep out dangerous enemies from the north.", "Although much of the wall has now disappeared, some remaining parts serve as memorials, reminding us of the great strength of ancient Chinese emperors and those who lost their lives during the wall’s building process.", "In Egypt, there are memorials that symbolize the strength of a nation’s ruler.", "Built thousands of years ago, the pyramids of Egypt were originally used to bury Egyptian kings and nobles.", "These amazing structures were filled with riches and offerings, and, of course, inside were the bodies for whom the structures were built.", "All these memorials impressed people at the time of their construction and still impress people today, showing us that they can stand the test of time without losing their importance."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the purpose of this passage?", "(A) To describe the beauty of famous memorials.", "(B) To discuss the importance of famous memorials.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) To explain the original functions of famous memorials.</strong>", "(D) To remind people to visit famous memorials more often.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ D ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following statements is true?", "(A) Memorials are always built to honor someone or something.", "(B) The Taj Mahal was designed to keep out dangerous enemies.", "(C) The Great Wall of China is believed to symbolize freedom and friendship.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) The pyramids of Egypt were built to show the strength of the country’s rulers.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t3.\tWhat is the author’s opinion about these memorials?", "(A) They are not as amazing as we think.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) They are significant and worth a visit.</strong>", "(C) They were only created to celebrate festivals.", "(D) They can be dangerous to visitors if not maintained well."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["Refund and Exchange Policy", "If you are not 100% satisfied with any of our products, please follow our refund and exchange policy.", "1. The product you purchased and the receipt are needed.", "2. The product must be unused and in the same condition as when you purchased it.", "Exchange", "You have 21 days to exchange a product after the date you purchased it.", "You can exchange the unwanted item for any product, but not for gift cards.", "Refunds", "If you purchased an item using cash, the refund will be in cash.", "If you purchased something using a credit/bank card, we will issue a refund to your card, which will take 3-5 business days.", "No refunds will be offered more than 14 days after your purchase.", "Contact Us", "If you have any questions regarding how to return an item or get a refund, please contact us."], "questions": ["When a product doesn’t (1)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">satisfy</strong>    your needs, note the purchase date and the payment method, so you will know when and how your money will be (2)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">refunded</strong>   .", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are true for the refund and exchange policy.       <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">C F</strong>", "(A) Although you cannot find the receipt, you can still exchange a product.", "(B) If the product breaks after use, you can exchange it.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) You cannot exchange your purchase for a gift card.</strong>", "(D) Even though you pay by credit card, you can get your refund in cash.", "(E) March 22 is the last day you can return a product you bought on March 1 and get a refund for it.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(F) If the company gets your returned item this Thursday, you can get a refund to your bank card next week.</strong>", "3.\tWhich word in the text means “to give something and receive another item in return”? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">exchange</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "L07": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["For students with musical potential, schools should offer special classes to help their talent develop.", "Wisdom is an invaluable gift that can only be gained through experience.", "I surely remember sending that letter; I don’t know why you didn’t receive it.", "With hard work and determination, the young tennis player improved greatly in a short time.", "About 30,000 fans cheered as their team walked off the field in triumph after winning the game.", "Monica was in such a hurry to catch the bus that I barely had a chance to talk with her.", "This medicine will make you feel dizzy and sleepy, so don’t drive after using it.", "Michael Jackson once dazzled millions of people around the globe with his classic moonwalk.", "We had a lot of fun at the party, but smoking was allowed there and somehow ruined our mood.", "In today’s science class, we used various instruments like thermometers and microscopes to conduct experiments."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["The little boy screamed in fear when a big dog barked at him.", "My grandfather taught me that the pursuit of knowledge and truth should be a lifelong journey.", "Peter is a faithful friend of mine.", "He always gives me a hand when I need help.", "I’m not surprised that hundreds of applicants came to the interview because this job offers a high salary.", "When Nancy failed the exam, her teacher did not scold her.", "Instead, he encouraged her to study harder."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["The boss asked me to have his car washed by 3:00 p.m.", "Percy will have the birthday cake baked before Rachel comes home.", "My CD player is broken, and I’m going to have it fixed.", "Robert had a bunch of roses sent to his wife on her birthday.", "The lady asked the manager when to start working.", "Peter hasn’t decided where to spend his vacation.", "Mark doesn’t know how to make conversation with a foreigner.", "Most high school students don’t like to be told what to do all the time.", "I’ll find out who to talk to about the budget for this project."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The boss asked me to have his car washed by 3:00 p.m</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Percy will have the birthday cake baked before Rachel comes home</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">My CD player is broken, and I’m going to have it fixed</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Robert had a bunch of roses sent to his wife on her birthday</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The lady asked the manager when to start working</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Peter hasn’t decided where to spend his vacation</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Mark doesn’t know how to make conversation with a foreigner</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Most high school students don’t like to be told what to do all the time</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I’ll find out who to talk to about the budget for this project</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["For more opportunities, Jason moved to a big city to look for a job.", "As a freelance writer, Tina makes/made a living by selling her articles to some publishers.", "The news that the concert has been cancelled because of the typhoon has depressed the boys, who have been looking forward to it for a long time.", "Sam didn’t have his car fixed, so he had to give up his plan to go on a road trip with Linda.", "Harry didn’t know how to tell his mother (that) his bicycle had been stolen.", "You should remember that worrying about failure doesn’t help anything.", "Keep trying, and you’ll be able to succeed one/some day."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Sam didn’t have his car fixed, so he had to give up his plan to go on a road trip with</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Linda</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Harry didn’t know how to tell his mother (that) his bicycle had been stolen</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">You should remember that worrying about failure doesn’t help anything</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Keep trying, and you’ll be able to succeed one/some day</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["El Sistema is a music program that began in the South American country of Venezuela.", "It was founded in 1975 by musician José Antonio Abreu, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) who</strong> designed the program to help poor children in the country.", "The program is based on the idea that change can <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (C) come out of</strong> music education—through music, young people can learn important life skills.", "Since its introduction in Venezuela, it has spread <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) overseas</strong> and inspired similar programs in more than 60 other countries.", "Children in the El Sistema program usually start learning music from a very early age.", "They learn <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) how</strong> to play instruments and sing.", "However, El Sistema appears to benefit kids not only <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) by</strong> providing them with a musical education.", "Many children in the program also manage <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (B) to improve</strong> their performance in various other school subjects.", "El Sistema is dedicated to supporting the development of youth orchestras.", "The program has had more than 100 youth orchestras <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (C) created</strong> in Venezuela.", "Many of them have played <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) concerts</strong> all over the world.", "Some orchestra members who are particularly <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) good at</strong> classical music have even become world-famous musicians!", "In summary, Venezuela’s El Sistema program uses music to help children find <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (D) what</strong> can change their life, become more confident, and develop into successfully functioning adults.", "The program is building a better future for young people both in Venezuela and beyond."], "questions": [], "source": ["El Sistema is a music program that began in the South American country of Venezuela*. It was founded in 1975 by musician José Antonio Abreu,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) who</strong>   designed the program to help poor children in the country. The program is based on the idea that change can   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (C) come out of</strong>   music education—through music, young people can learn important life skills. Since its introduction in Venezuela, it has spread   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) overseas</strong>   and inspired similar programs in more than 60 other countries.", "Children in the El Sistema program usually start learning music from a very early age. They learn   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) how</strong>   to play instruments and sing. However, El Sistema appears to benefit kids not only   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) by</strong>   providing them with a musical education. Many children in the program also manage   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (B) to improve</strong>   their performance in various other school subjects.", "El Sistema is dedicated* to supporting the development of youth orchestras. The program has had more than 100 youth orchestras   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (C) created</strong>   in Venezuela. Many of them have played   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) concerts</strong>   all over the world. Some orchestra members who are particularly", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) good at</strong>   classical music have even become world-famous musicians!", "In summary, Venezuela’s El Sistema program uses music to help children find   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (D) what</strong>   \ncan change their life, become more confident, and develop into successfully functioning adults. The program is building a better future for young people both in Venezuela and beyond.", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["The story of Ugandan chess star Phiona Mutesi is a true rags-to-riches tale.", "Mutesi grew up in Katwe, a slum in Kampala, Uganda’s capital.", "When she was young, her family struggled with extreme poverty, and they could <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) barely</strong> afford to send her to school on a regular basis.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (G) Fortunately</strong>, one day, when she was nine years old, she discovered an after-school sports program that was run by a local coach.", "It was through this program that Mutesi <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (A) received</strong> a chess education.", "She greatly enjoyed playing chess and was <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (I) good</strong> at it.", "She seemed to have considerable <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (E) potential</strong> as a player.", "Over the next few years, although Mutesi regularly went without proper meals because of her family’s situation, she continued to <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (B) improve</strong> at chess.", "Before long, she was competing and enjoying success in chess events both in Uganda and <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (H) overseas</strong>.", "Today, Mutesi is viewed as a symbol of hope that <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (J) encourages</strong> children living in poverty all over the world.", "In 2012, a book was written about her, and it was made into a movie in 2016.", "In 2017, her <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (F) application</strong> for a scholarship to study at Northwest University in the US was accepted.", "While she was studying there, she competed in a number of events with the university’s chess team and won several titles.", "Mutesi’s story shows that with <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (D) determination</strong> and hard work, anyone can realize his or her dream, no matter where he or she starts."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "The story of Ugandan* chess star Phiona Mutesi is a true rags-to-riches* tale. Mutesi grew up in Katwe, a slum in Kampala, Uganda’s capital. When she was young, her family struggled with extreme poverty, and they could   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) barely</strong>   afford to send her to school on a regular basis.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (G) fortunately</strong>  , one day, when she was nine years old, she discovered an after-school sports program that was run by a local coach. It was through this program that Mutesi   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (A) received</strong>   a chess education. She greatly enjoyed playing chess and was   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (I) good</strong>   at it. She seemed to have considerable   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (E) potential</strong>   as a player.", "Over the next few years, although Mutesi regularly went without proper meals because of her family’s situation, she continued to   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (B) improve</strong>   at chess. Before long, she was competing and enjoying success in chess events both in Uganda and   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (H) overseas</strong>  .", "Today, Mutesi is viewed as a symbol of hope that   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (J) encourages</strong>   children living in poverty all over the world. In 2012, a book was written about her, and it was made into a movie in 2016. In 2017, her   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (F) application</strong>   for a scholarship to study at Northwest University in the US was accepted. While she was studying there, she competed in a number of events with the university’s chess team and won several titles. Mutesi’s story shows that with   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (D) determination</strong>   \nand hard work, anyone can realize his or her dream, no matter where he or she starts.", null, null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["I have been running a restaurant next to a big university for the past twenty years.", "Soon after my restaurant opened, I met a young man who then started to come in every day at lunchtime.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) He would always order the same thing: two bowls of rice with some braised pork sauce</strong>.", "That was all; nothing else.", "The handsome young man seemed to be a student, but his book bag, shoes, and clothes all looked old and dirty.", "Several weeks later, I told my wife about this customer.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) We agreed that he was probably poor and unable to afford any meat or vegetables</strong>.", "We felt very sorry for him because he reminded us of our own son.", "The next day, I filled a lunchbox with meat and vegetables for him and put it into his take-out bag along with the rice.", "He tried to pay me for this additional food, but I refused to take the extra money.", "He left looking extremely grateful.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) Each day after that, he came back and ordered rice, but I would always make sure that he left with a variety of other foods</strong>.", "Later, I found out that this student was a very hardworking engineering student who dreamed of starting his own technology company.", "After he graduated from the university, I didn’t hear from him for a long time.", "However, one day more than fifteen years later, he suddenly came back, surrounded by reporters.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) It turned out that he had become one of the wealthiest men in the nation, and he had told the media about how my restaurant had helped him survive through his college days</strong>!", "Now, my business is better than ever, and people come from all around the country to try my food.", "Indeed, what goes around comes around."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, "I have been running a restaurant next to a big university for the past twenty years. Soon after my restaurant opened, I met a young man who then started to come in every day at lunchtime.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) He would always order the same thing: two bowls of rice with some braised pork sauce.</strong>   That was all; nothing else. The handsome young man seemed to be a student, but his book bag, shoes, and clothes all looked old and dirty.", "Several weeks later, I told my wife about this customer.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) We agreed that he was probably poor and unable to afford any meat or vegetables.</strong>   We felt very sorry for him because he reminded us of our own son. The next day, I filled a lunchbox with meat and vegetables for him and put it into his take-out bag along with the rice. He tried to pay me for this additional food, but I refused to take the extra money. He left looking extremely grateful*.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) Each day after that, he came back and ordered rice, but I would always make sure that he left with a variety of other foods.</strong>", "Later, I found out that this student was a very hardworking engineering student who dreamed of starting his own technology company. After he graduated from the university, I didn’t hear from him for a long time. However, one day more than fifteen years later, he suddenly came back, surrounded by reporters.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) It turned out that he had become one of the wealthiest men in the nation, and he had told the media about how my restaurant had helped him survive through his college days!</strong>   Now, my business is better than ever, and people come from all around the country to try my food. Indeed, what goes around comes around.", null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["In Paraguay, there is a really cool structure called the Itaipu Dam.", "It looks like a massive wall built on the Paraná River.", "However, more than a typical wall, it helps make electricity without hurting our planet.", "It is actually the second-largest hydroelectric power plant in the world.", "The Itaipu Dam was built from 1971 to 1984.", "It was a large project that cost over $19 billion.", "Paraguay and its neighbor, Brazil, both worked together to build it.", "The end result was a dam that is 8 km long and uses the power of the river’s water to spin big turbines, which are giant wheels that make electricity.", "The dam helps light up homes, schools, and cities in Paraguay.", "In fact, it is so powerful that it supplies around 90% of the country’s electricity.", "What’s really fabulous about the Itaipu Dam is that it is eco-friendly.", "It doesn’t harm the environment like some other power plants might.", "Instead, it shows us how we can use nature’s resources smartly to provide power without making a mess of the environment.", "In short, the Itaipu Dam is a big, important structure in Paraguay.", "It helps create electricity for lots of people and does it in a way that is good for our planet.", "It is like a super-powered green machine that makes our world a brighter place."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ A ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is this passage mainly about?", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(A) The features of a power plant.</strong>", "(B) The process of planning a power plant.", "(C) The functions of an ordinary power plant.", "(D) The necessity of building eco-friendly power plants.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following statements is true?", "(A) Paraguay built the Itaipu Dam on its own.", "(B) The Itaipu Dam looks like a tower on the river.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) The Itaipu Dam is good for Paraguayans and the environment.</strong>", "(D) The Itaipu Dam supplies half of the electricity that Paraguay needs.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ D ）</strong>\t3.\tWhich of the following is closest in meaning to the word “fabulous” in the third paragraph?", "(A) proper", "(B) typical", "(C) ordinary", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) amazing</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["The Ant and the Grasshopper (adapted from Aesop’s Fables) One day in summer, Grasshopper was hopping and singing in a field.", "Then, he saw Ant walking by.", "Ant was taking an ear of corn back to his nest.", "“Hi there, Ant!", "What are you doing?", "Why don’t you hang out with me?”", "Grasshopper asked.", "“No, thanks.", "I’m preparing food for winter, and I suggest you do the same,” Ant replied.", "“Prepare for winter?", "Why?", "Winter is six months from now, and we still have a lot of food to eat!” said Grasshopper.", "Ant ignored Grasshopper and kept carrying the corn.", "When winter came, Grasshopper found that there was nothing left for him to eat.", "Just when he was about to die, he saw that the ants were eating the food they had stored in the summer.", "Only then did Grasshopper realize that it is always best to prepare for the days of necessity."], "questions": ["The story teaches us the importance of taking wise (1) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">suggestions</strong>   from other people, which may help us avoid a serious danger, such as (2)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">death</strong>    .", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are true for the story.        <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">C F</strong>", "(A) Grasshopper talked with Ant because he wanted to help.", "(B) Ant didn’t hang out with Grasshopper because he was shy.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) Ant didn’t accept Grasshopper’s invitation.</strong>", "(D) Both Ant and Grasshopper had enough food to get through the winter.", "(E) The climax was when Grasshopper finally realized it is better to prepare for the future.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(F) Grasshopper is the main character in the story.</strong>", "3.\tWhich word in the story means “refused to notice”? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">ignored</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "L08": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["Tina always comes up with clever ideas to help her clients solve their difficulties.", "Dave is a heavy drinker, and it is hard for him to control his urge to drink alcohol.", "Height is an advantage in many sports, including basketball, volleyball, and swimming.", "The new guy in the office is not familiar with the copy machine at all.", "He can’t even find the start button.", "The team are aware of the problem they are facing and are trying hard to deal with it.", "A 21-year-old man cleaned the road signs voluntarily to make them clearly visible again and help people drive safely.", "The salesman allowed his customer to try out the machine for several days before buying it.", "If we want to win the baseball game, we have to work out a strategy for handling this situation.", "None of us have any doubt that Dick will eventually succeed, for he has great talent and works extremely hard.", "When Shelly heard the good news, she had a sudden impulse to dance in front of all the people."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["The similarity between Tom and his elder brother James is very striking.", "Over 2,000 valuable Chinese artifacts are on display in the museum right now.", "Hundreds of people were trapped in the fallen building during the earthquake.", "An advantage of using a credit card is that you can charge most purchases without paying for them right away.", "Mike is happy to see his company’s profits rising every year."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["The older Van gets, the more hair he loses.", "The warmer the weather is, the faster the plant grows.", "The more junk food you eat, the fatter you will become.", "The better prepared you are, the more likely you’ll be to succeed.", "The more information you gather, the easier it will be for you to make a decision.", "Jenny is going for a walk so that she can get some fresh air.", "The old man put on his glasses so that he could read the small print in the newspaper.", "Mr. Chen and his wife left early so that they wouldn’t be late for the party.", "Mr. Lee decided to quit smoking so that he could lead a healthier life."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The older Van gets, the more hair he loses</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The warmer the weather is, the faster the plant grows</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The more junk food you eat, the fatter you will become</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The better prepared you are, the more likely you’ll be to succeed</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The more information you gather, the easier it will be for you to make a decision</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Jenny is going for a walk so that she can get some fresh air</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The old man put on his glasses so that he could read the small print in the newspaper</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Mr. Chen and his wife left early so that they wouldn’t be late for the party</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Mr. Lee decided to quit smoking so that he could lead a healthier life</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["All the passengers lined up to board the ship to Kaohsiung, which was leaving in an hour.", "Larry will need to have enough money before he thinks about setting up a company.", "Tom took advantage of the good weather to paint the fence.", "Jasmine learned Japanese so that she could study Japanese films more efficiently.", "There is no need to worry about that test. If you study hard, you’re likely to pass it.", "It is believed that the more friends you have, the happier you are.", "However, you should try to avoid hanging out with bad friends so that you don’t/won’t get into trouble."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Jasmine learned Japanese so that she could study Japanese films more efficiently</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">There is no need to worry about that test. If you study hard, you’re likely to pass it</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is believed that the more friends you have, the happier you are</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">However, you should try to avoid hanging out with bad friends so that you don’t/won’t</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">get into trouble</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["From supermarkets to shopping malls, stores use many strategies to make us spend more money.", "That is, they design their stores in particular ways <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) so that</strong> you will hand over more of the cash in your pocket.", "For example, it’s common to see a big red sign <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (C) that</strong> says “Sale.”", "These signs make the shop seem <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) attractive</strong> because the color red encourages people to make quicker decisions.", "Inside the shop, the colors most commonly used are blue and green because these colors help create a relaxing atmosphere.", "Besides colors, store clerks are sure to tell shoppers that their special deals are available for only a short time.", "They do this to make shoppers <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) feel</strong> pressure to buy immediately.", "In addition, many big stores, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (A) such as</strong> Carrefour, also have big empty shopping carts.", "Studies have shown that bigger shopping carts may trick customers into spending more.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) Therefore</strong>, shoppers will want to fill their carts with more stuff.", "Supermarkets also know what to put at the front of the store.", "They always <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) place</strong> colorful fruit near the door because seeing it puts shoppers in a good mood.", "Similarly, baked goods and other treats that you enjoy smelling are near the front.", "Smelling something pleasant increases the chances of buying items <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (D) on</strong> impulse.", "Moreover, because <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) the most</strong> popular items are at the back of the supermarket, shoppers have to walk across the whole store to find them.", "They may end up <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (A) being</strong> tempted to buy extra items.", "So, keep these marketing strategies in mind if you need to spend less the next time you are shopping.", "In other words, be careful when you shop!"], "questions": [], "source": ["From supermarkets to shopping malls, stores use many strategies to make us spend more money. That is, they design their stores in particular ways   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (A) so that</strong>   you will hand over more of the cash in your pocket. For example, it’s common to see a big red sign   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (C) that</strong>   \nsays “Sale.” These signs make the shop seem   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) attractive</strong>   because the color red encourages people to make quicker decisions. Inside the shop, the colors most commonly used are blue and green because these colors help create a relaxing atmosphere. Besides colors, store clerks are sure to tell shoppers that their special deals are available for only a short time. They do this to make shoppers   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) feel</strong>   pressure to buy immediately. In addition, many big stores,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (A) such as</strong>   Carrefour, also have big empty shopping carts. Studies have shown that bigger shopping carts may trick customers into spending more.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) Therefore</strong>   , shoppers will want to fill their carts with more stuff. Supermarkets also know what to put at the front of the store. They always   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) place</strong>   colorful fruit near the door because seeing it puts shoppers in a good mood. Similarly, baked goods and other treats that you enjoy smelling are near the front. Smelling something pleasant increases the chances of buying items   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (D) on</strong>   impulse.", "Moreover, because   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) the most</strong>   popular items are at the back of the supermarket, shoppers have to walk across the whole store to find them. They may end up   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (A) being</strong>   tempted to buy extra items. So, keep these marketing strategies in mind if you need to spend less the next time you are shopping. In other words, be careful when you shop!", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["People today are exposed to advertising in many forms.", "Most ads are <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) visible</strong>, but some, like radio ads, are not.", "Nevertheless, whatever form they come in, advertisements work, and that is why we should try to be more <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) aware</strong> of them.", "As consumers, we need to realize that ads are always trying to make us buy something.", "They also <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (J) aim</strong> to influence the way we think.", "Sometimes, they even set <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) traps</strong> for us and make products appear better than they really are.", "To avoid <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (H) falling</strong> into these traps, we need to slow down and think about why advertisements are so effective.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) In addition</strong>, we need to dig deeper into all the tricks they use to influence their specific target markets.", "Ads for make-up at store counters, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (F) for example</strong>, often feature popular celebrities to make people think that they will look just as good as these stars if they use the same products.", "Seeing these glamorous advertisements, customers waiting in line to <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (I) pay</strong> often can’t resist adding these items to their baskets.", "They have just made a(n) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) impulse</strong> purchase, but will it really make them look like a star?", "Remember that only by remaining alert to all these different sales <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (G) strategies</strong> can you avoid buying things you don’t really need.", "Finally, given that it pays to advertise, don’t forget to warn all your friends, too!"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "People today are exposed to advertising in many forms. Most ads are   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) visible</strong>  , but some, like radio ads, are not.", "Nevertheless, whatever form they come in, advertisements work, and that is why we should try to be more   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) aware</strong>   of them. As consumers, we need to realize that ads are always trying to make us buy something. They also   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (J) aim</strong>   to influence the way we think. Sometimes, they even set   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) traps</strong>   for us and make products appear better than they really are. To avoid   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (H) falling</strong>   into these traps, we need to slow down and think about why advertisements are so effective.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) in addition</strong>  , we need to dig deeper into all the tricks they use to influence their specific target markets. Ads for make-up at store counters,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (F) for example</strong>  , often feature popular celebrities to make people think that they will look just as good as these stars if they use the same products. Seeing these glamorous advertisements, customers waiting in line to   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (I) pay</strong>   often can’t resist adding these items to their baskets. They have just made a(n)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (C) impulse</strong>   purchase, but will it really make them look like a star?", "Remember that only by remaining alert to all these different sales   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (G) strategies</strong>   can you avoid buying things you don’t really need. Finally, given that it pays to advertise, don’t forget to warn all your friends, too!", null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["Big companies like Costco use a number of strategies to lure customers into purchasing their goods.", "The first is the members-only strategy, meaning that only members can buy goods or receive discounts.", "Membership is attractive because it creates a sense of ownership and belonging for customers.", "They may feel more special or more valued than other people if they receive special treatment as members of a specific club or store.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) To maintain such a membership, however, customers must pay a yearly fee or spend a certain amount each year</strong>.", "The second strategy is the “buy in large amounts and save” strategy.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) In other words, the more you buy, the lower the price is</strong>.", "Large retailers use this strategy to get customers to spend more while keeping their own costs low at the same time.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) However, in order to receive discounted pricing, some customers may end up buying more than they need and thus waste their money</strong>.", "The third strategy that encourages customers to spend more involves holiday deals offered by large stores.", "Such seasonal sales give customers another reason to buy things even when they don’t really need to.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) They take advantage of traditional celebrations such as Thanksgiving, Christmas, and Chinese New Year to encourage people to spend even more on gifts, food, and decorations</strong>.", "At times, certain holiday deals are purely meant to lure people into buying more.", "One example is “Black Friday,” when prices are often cut dramatically so that people will want to buy more items and thus spend more money."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, "Big companies like Costco use a number of strategies to lure* customers into purchasing their goods. The first is the members-only strategy, meaning that only members can buy goods or receive discounts. Membership is attractive because it creates a sense of ownership and belonging for customers. They may feel more special or more valued than other people if they receive special treatment as members of a specific club or store.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) To maintain such a membership, however, customers must pay a yearly fee or spend a certain amount each year.</strong>", "The second strategy is the “buy in large amounts and save” strategy.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) In other words, the more you buy, the lower the price is.</strong>   Large retailers use this strategy to get customers to spend more while keeping their own costs low at the same time.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) However, in order to receive discounted pricing, some customers may end up buying more than they need and thus waste their money.</strong>", "The third strategy that encourages customers to spend more involves holiday deals offered by large stores. Such seasonal sales give customers another reason to buy things even when they don’t really need to.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (E) They take advantage of traditional celebrations such as Thanksgiving, Christmas, and Chinese New Year to encourage people to spend even more on gifts, food, and decorations.</strong>   At times, certain holiday deals are purely meant to lure people into buying more. One example is “Black Friday,” when prices are often cut dramatically so that people will want to buy more items and thus spend more money.", null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["The latest technology seems to never stop showing up in our daily lives.", "This reality is particularly evident in Amazon’s latest take on the grocery store: Amazon Go.", "Amazon Go is a new style of grocery store that allows shoppers to take out their phone, sign in to the Amazon Go app, and run the phone over a sensor bar as they walk into the store.", "After that, a shopper can put their phone away, shop as they like, and then walk out without needing to wait in a checkout line or pay at a register.", "When customers are shopping in an Amazon Go store, every item they pick up is put into their virtual cart.", "They can choose from everyday goods, such as milk and eggs, to more special items, such as prepared meals and sandwiches, take-home meals created by in-house chefs, and locally produced cheeses and chocolate.", "Everything that is taken off the shelf is saved in their app, and they are charged automatically and sent an e-receipt in the app after they walk out.", "Amazon Go makes this shopping experience possible by using some of the newest technology available, including computer vision, deep learning algorithms, and sensor fusion.", "Amazon has named this technology, which is similar to what is used in self-driving cars, “Just Walk Out” technology, and it is certain to change the shopping experience as we know it."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat kind of passage is this?", "(A) A film review.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) A news report.</strong>", "(C) A story narration.", "(D) A historical study.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following is NOT mentioned as a potential benefit of Amazon Go?", "(A) People can shop without waiting in line to pay.", "(B) People can choose from daily items to more special items.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) People can get anything they need without going into a store.</strong>", "(D) People will be charged automatically and get an e-receipt after shopping.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ D ）</strong>\t3.\tWhat is true about Amazon Go?", "(A) It saves people money on shopping.", "(B) It is a great new type of department store.", "(C) It allows people to shop without leaving their house.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) It uses a technology like that used in self-driving cars.</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["BENEFITS OF ONLINE SHOPPING There are many benefits of online shopping.", "Compared with traditional shopping, it is more convenient, it saves time, there is less sales pressure, and prices are generally lower.", "However, there are also some disadvantages.", "For example, items may be over-packaged for shipping.", "So, be smart when you shop and enjoy the benefits.", "#CONVENIENT You can shop anytime, even in the middle of the night from your comfortable bed.", "#TIME-SAVING It takes only a few clicks to shop.", "It is even closer than the convenience store on the corner.", "#LESS SALES PRESSURE There are no other customers or shopkeepers around you pushing you to hurry or to buy items you don’t need.", "#BETTER PRICES It’s easy to find lower prices and second- hand items.", "Just be sure of what you really need and choose a reliable online store.", "Then, you can be a smart online shopper."], "questions": ["Although online shopping can (1)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">benefit</strong>    shoppers in many ways, they still should understand their real needs and find online stores that they can (2)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">rely</strong>     \non.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are NOT mentioned as benefits of online shopping in the text.      <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">C F</strong>", "(A) It’s easy to find better prices at online stores.", "(B) You can shop from home with just a few clicks.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) Clerks are always ready to offer advice and suggestions.</strong>", "(D) There is no one to push you to buy more than you need.", "(E) Online stores are open 24/7 every day.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(F) Goods can be delivered to your address quickly.</strong>", "3.\tWhich word in the text means “things that cause problems”? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">disadvantages</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "L09": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["If you don’t put in enough effort, you won’t learn a foreign language.", "Patty looked with horror at the giant snake on the road.", "The movie’s dialogue was dull, but the visual effects were amazing.", "The news report said a dangerous criminal had just escaped from prison.", "The man just moved to our community a week ago, so I don’t know him very well.", "A good learner often associates what he is learning with what he already knows.", "Many parents do not want their children to watch movies that contain too much violence.", "This satellite takes such detailed pictures of the ground that you can see people’s faces in them.", "Julie expressed surprise when I told her Jimmy was coming to visit us this afternoon.", "The two countries failed to reach an agreement because they held different opinions on economic issues."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["If we continue to pollute the environment we live in, it will soon influence our health.", "My dad permitted me to use his iPad today because he didn’t need it for his work.", "A strong typhoon knocked down several buildings and caused destruction throughout the town.", "Andy’s politeness is in sharp contrast to his brother’s rude behavior.", "They’re so different from each other.", "I tried to prove to the police that I was innocent of the crime by providing an alibi (不在場證明)."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["Jason looked out the window, enjoying the beautiful view.", "The boy got on the school bus, carrying some books under his arm.", "The little girl went into the theater, accompanied by her mother.", "Dennis froze in front of the class, not knowing how to answer the question.", "The woman looked at the old photo, lost in thought.", "I drink black coffee, while/whereas my brother prefers coffee with cream.", "Some countries are very rich, while/whereas others are extremely poor.", "That area has a lot of natural resources, while/whereas this area has none.", "Tom often hangs out with his friends, while/whereas Ted usually stays at home alone."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Jason looked out the window, enjoying the beautiful view</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The boy got on the school bus, carrying some books under his arm</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The little girl went into the theater, accompanied by her mother</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Dennis froze in front of the class, not knowing how to answer the question</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The woman looked at the old photo, lost in thought</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I drink black coffee, while/whereas my brother prefers coffee with cream</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Some countries are very rich, while/whereas others are extremely poor</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">That area has a lot of natural resources, while/whereas this area has none</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Tom often hangs out with his friends, while/whereas Ted usually stays at home</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">alone</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["This car model comes in three different colors for you to choose from.", "I have nothing but a sweater to keep myself warm, so let’s not stay outside too long.", "If you want to get rid of body fat, you should have a well-balanced diet.", "When it comes to taste in music, Frank’s is obviously different from Jack’s.", "Red roses stand for love. If I fall in love with a girl, I will give one to her to show my love.", "Although the news reports have called the public’s attention to graffiti, many people still don’t really care about this issue.", "They contrast it with other social problems, feeling that it is only a minor issue."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">When it comes to taste in music, Frank’s is obviously different from Jack’s</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Red roses stand for love. If I fall in love with a girl, I will give one to her to show my \t\nlove</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Although the news reports have called the public’s attention to graffiti, many people still</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">don’t really care about this issue</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">They contrast it with other social problems, feeling that it is only a minor issue</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["On Thursday night, famous graffiti artist Matt Garner will be giving a talk about graffiti at New State College.", "Matt is a talented artist <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) who</strong> paints street art under the nickname “Paladin.”", "Some people love his works, while <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) others</strong> see them as a coward’s art.", "Through this talk, he hopes to change people’s minds about this art form <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) which</strong> so few understand.", "Paladin’s art is mostly political.", "He likes to compare the media’s descriptions of war <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) with</strong> the real-life effects of conflict.", "His most famous work is Sugar-Free Will, which shows <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) millions of</strong> television audience members staring wide-eyed at a handsome actor on a screen.", "This piece <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) calls</strong> our attention to the political platform that Hollywood actors use to spread their personal views.", "Those who don’t like Paladin’s art say that <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) rather than</strong> solving problems, his graffiti creates new ones.", "Such people argue that Paladin encourages crime and that works like his <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) make</strong> the city look messy.", "However, supporters point out that his art makes neighborhoods more beautiful, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) decorating</strong> them with interesting images.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (D) In addition</strong>, they argue that artists have used art to spread political messages for centuries, so Paladin is doing what an artist should do.", "No matter what your views are, come and listen to Matt’s thoughts on the subject.", "At the end of the speech, there will be an open discussion for the audience, so you’ll have a chance to express your thoughts.", "Hope to see you there!"], "questions": [], "source": ["On Thursday night, famous graffiti artist Matt Garner will be giving a talk about graffiti at New State College. Matt is a talented artist   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) who</strong>   paints street art under the nickname “Paladin.” Some people love his works, while   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) others</strong>   see them as a coward’s art. Through this talk, he hopes to change people’s minds about this art form   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) which</strong>   so few understand.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (A) with</strong>   the real-life effects of conflict. His most famous work is Sugar-Free Will, which shows   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) millions of</strong>   television audience members staring wide-eyed at a handsome actor on a screen. This piece   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (D) calls</strong>   our attention to the political platform that Hollywood actors use to spread their personal views.", "Those who don’t like Paladin’s art say that   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) rather than</strong>   solving problems, his graffiti creates new ones. Such people argue that Paladin encourages crime and that works like his", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) make</strong>   the city look messy. However, supporters point out that his art makes neighborhoods", "more beautiful,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) decorating</strong>   them with interesting images.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (D) In addition</strong>  , they argue that artists have used art to spread political messages for centuries, so Paladin is doing what an artist should do.", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "文意選填": {"pairs": ["Society is governed by law.", "If nobody enforced rules, the sense of <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) community</strong> we feel through living close to one another would not exist, nor would society be able to function.", "This is why preventing <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) crime</strong>, however minor, is so important.", "Even not so serious offenses—like creating graffiti, in my <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (H) opinion</strong> —should be policed very strictly.", "The authorities should, therefore, try just as hard to prevent such offenses as they can to prevent acts of theft or <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) violence</strong>.", "Graffiti that is not officially allowed or approved destroys private or state property, and it often takes a lot of time and effort and costs a lot of money to wash it <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (F) away</strong>.", "Of course, I agree that graffiti can be seen as a form of artistic <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (J) expression</strong>.", "However, I also think that artists who wish to express themselves through this type of <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (A) visual</strong> art should consider other ways of doing so.", "They could, for example, transfer their views and ideas <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (D) onto</strong> the walls inside their own homes and then invite others to come and see and discuss their work.", "At the end of the day, when graffiti is created without the <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (G) permission</strong> of the public and the government, it is not a legal act.", "No wonder most people are so strongly <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (I) against</strong> it.", "If graffiti artists really want their artwork to be appreciated and their messages to be heard, they should look at the big picture and try to get society on their side first."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "Society is governed by law. If nobody enforced rules, the sense of   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) community</strong>   we feel through living close to one another would not exist, nor would society be able to function. This is why preventing   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (E) crime</strong>  , however minor, is so important.", "Even not so serious offenses—like creating graffiti, in my   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (H) opinion</strong>  —should be policed very strictly. The authorities should, therefore, try just as hard to prevent such offenses as they can to prevent acts of theft or   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) violence</strong>  . Graffiti that is not officially allowed or approved destroys private or state property, and it often takes a lot of time and effort and costs a lot of money to wash it   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (F) away</strong>  .", "Of course, I agree that graffiti can be seen as a form of artistic   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (J) expression</strong>  . However, I also think that artists who wish to express themselves through this type of   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (A) visual</strong>   art should consider other ways of doing so. They could, for example, transfer their views and ideas   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (D) onto</strong>   the walls inside their own homes and then invite others to come and see and discuss their work.", "At the end of the day, when graffiti is created without the   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (G) permission</strong>   of the public and the government, it is not a legal act. No wonder most people are so strongly   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (I) against</strong>   it. If graffiti artists really want their artwork to be appreciated and their messages to be heard, they should look at the big picture and try to get society on their side first.", null, null]}, "篇章結構": {"pairs": ["Throughout history, people have used technology to solve health problems.", "Despite major advances, developments, and inventions, however, one problem has only become worse over time.", "This problem is obesity.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (E) Recent years have seen increased rates of weight gain and disease related to obesity in countries all around the world</strong>.", "In the United States, for example, over 70% of all adults aged 20 and over are now overweight or obese.", "Scientists are fiercely debating whether diet or lack of physical activity is more to blame.", "Those who say diet is to blame often point to processed foods.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) This is because such foods tend to contain a lot of sugar and fat</strong>.", "Moreover, processed foods often require little preparation, so children or adults who are unable to cook or prepare their own meals are more likely to purchase them.", "What’s even worse is that unhealthy processed foods are often cheaper than healthy, natural products, which makes people even more likely to purchase them.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) On the other hand, those who say a lack of exercise is the cause of obesity often blame the modern lifestyle</strong>.", "Many of today’s kids, for example, spend more time playing computer games at home than playing outside.", "Additionally, cars, buses, and trains now enable us to travel long distances easily, but they also mean we walk far less than our ancestors did.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) Finally, many modern jobs require workers to sit for long hours at desks</strong>.", "All these factors have one thing in common: They lead to less physical activity and less exercise.", "So, which factor do you think is to blame, diet or lifestyle?"], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, "Throughout history, people have used technology to solve health problems. Despite major advances, developments, and inventions, however, one problem has only become worse over time. This problem is obesity*.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (E) Recent years have seen increased rates of weight gain and disease related to obesity in countries all around the world.</strong>   In the United States, for example, over 70% of all adults aged 20 and over are now overweight or obese. Scientists are fiercely debating* whether diet or lack of physical activity is more to blame.", "Those who say diet is to blame often point to processed foods.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (A) This is because such foods tend to contain a lot of sugar and fat.</strong>   Moreover, processed foods often require little preparation, so children or adults who are unable to cook or prepare their own meals are more likely to purchase them. What’s even worse is that unhealthy processed foods are often cheaper than healthy, natural products, which makes people even more likely to purchase them.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (D) On the other hand, those who say a lack of exercise is the cause of obesity often blame the modern lifestyle.</strong>   Many of today’s kids, for example, spend more time playing computer games at home than playing outside. Additionally, cars, buses, and trains now enable us to travel long distances easily, but they also mean we walk far less than our ancestors* did.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) Finally, many modern jobs require workers to sit for long hours at desks.</strong>   \nAll these factors have one thing in common: They lead to less physical activity and less exercise.", null, null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["Graffiti is a special art form that can serve various functions.", "It can mark a territory, express a political opinion, or show people a new visual world by creating complex designs that confuse the eye.", "It can also blend cultures and art styles and help an artist feel free.", "These days, graffiti can be found in cities in almost every country; however, the treatment it receives is not always the same.", "Graffiti is actually illegal in most places, but Bogota, Colombia, is a rare exception.", "This city has allowed graffiti since the public protested against a young graffiti artist being killed by the police in 2011.", "Since then, art on walls has been seen all over Bogota.", "More than eight thousand local artists there now create designs that show everything from Colombian culture to fantasy images.", "Zurich, Switzerland, is another city where graffiti artists can display their talent freely.", "At the Rote Fabrik, graffiti artists are not merely allowed but actually encouraged to spray the walls.", "To Zurich locals, graffiti is not an illegal act but an expression of freedom.", "In addition to the above two cities, graffiti artists can also display their talent in New York City, a city with a long history of graffiti related to hip hop culture and punk music.", "Most of the world’s famous graffiti artists have been to New York and created many famous art pieces there.", "In fact, graffiti exists almost everywhere in the city, from small tags with people’s names spray-painted on them to giant full-wall murals, like the Audubon Mural Project, which depicts birds that have fallen victim to climate change.", "Thanks to places like these cities, graffiti artists around the world have spaces to show their artwork and to help graffiti culture further develop."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t1.\tHow does the author start this passage?", "(A) By introducing some studies on graffiti.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) By introducing the functions of graffiti.</strong>", "(C) By giving some news about graffiti.", "(D) By comparing graffiti in different places.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ A ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following statements is true about graffiti art in New York City?", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(A) It has some connection with pop music.</strong>", "(B) People spray-paint their names on sidewalks.", "(C) Only some lesser-known artists have created works there.", "(D) The Audubon Mural Project aims to show birds suffering from hunger.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t3.\tWhat can we learn from the passage?", "(A) Graffiti is still unwelcome in Bogota, Columbia.", "(B) Graffiti is symbolic of love in Zurich, Switzerland.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) Graffiti artists in some cities are encouraged to keep developing their talent.</strong>", "(D) Wall art is popular in Bogota, with over 9,000 artists creating designs there."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["I love my adopted cats—Shining, Spottie, and Mucho—very much.", "They are noble and beautiful and have never caused any trouble for me or my furniture.", "I cannot understand why some people shop for cats at pet stores instead of adopting them from animal shelters.", "Don’t they know that pet stores cold-bloodedly force female cats and dogs to give birth to kittens and puppies?", "Buying animals from such stores actually supports this type of cruel behavior.", "By contrast, adopting a pet from a shelter saves a life because these animals are put to death if they stay at the shelter for a certain period.", "To survive, these little creatures need only a small space and food to eat.", "Moreover, after being adopted, they give you their unconditional love in return.", "So, don’t buy a pet at a store.", "Adopt one instead!"], "questions": ["Instead of buying cats and dogs at pet stores, we should support the (1)  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">adoption</strong>    \nof these furry friends from shelters to ensure their (2)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">survival</strong>   .", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that agree with the author’s attitude. <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">B D F</strong>", "(A) Iris: “It’s better to buy a pet from an actual store than online.”", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) Pete: “Adopting animals from animal shelters helps them live longer.”</strong>", "(C) Wayne: “Animals purchased in stores are less pretty than adopted ones.”", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) Ed: “Most pet stores think little about the health of female animals.”</strong>", "(E) Kim: “It doesn’t matter where you buy your pet as long as you love it.”", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(F) Ellen: “Fewer animals bought from pet stores means fewer animals will be abused.”</strong>", "3.\tWhich word in the text means “temporary safe places for homeless animals”? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">shelters</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "R01": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["Wendy held her breath as she checked the results of the entrance exam.", "Mike wanted his mother’s birthday party to be perfect, so he spent the whole week preparing for it.", "Skipping breakfast will do more harm than good to our health.", "We introduced ourselves in English to the exchange students from Canada.", "The man is incredibly lucky to have survived the plane crash.", "Studies show that many species of sharks and other sea animals may disappear very soon.", "I’ve decided to leave the US forever and return to Taiwan to live there for the rest of my life.", "Nothing is more valuable than family and friends.", "The students are all at the same level, so there shouldn’t be much difference in their abilities.", "Tom plays soccer with his friends every Saturday morning.", "Afterward, they always go and eat lunch together."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["The patient has been kept in ignorance of his own condition.", "The waiter greeted us with a smile when we went into the restaurant.", "People at the cultural festival were able to taste food from all around the world.", "The singer’s latest song was inspired by his new baby.", "The parents felt embarrassed when their children started laughing in the middle of the show."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["Reviewing lessons before class helps me learn better.", "If we hurry up, we may be able to see the sea of clouds.", "Jane exercises regularly in order to stay fit.", "I was allowed to use my brother’s computer when he wasn’t home.", "It is very interesting for me to go camping with my family.", "Sam wondered where Kevin bought that T-shirt.", "Judy has taken piano lessons since she was six years old.", "Something has to be done (by someone) before it is too late.", "You should make sure that there are still some tickets available for the opera tomorrow evening before going there."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Reviewing lessons before class helps me learn better</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">If we hurry up, we may be able to see the sea of clouds</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Jane exercises regularly in order to stay fit</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I was allowed to use my brother’s computer when he wasn’t home</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is very interesting for me to go camping with my family</strong>.", null, null, "Sam wondered <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">where Kevin bought that T-shirt</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Judy has taken piano lessons since she was six years old</strong>.", null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["Everything was fine on our hiking trip except for the weather.", "Ellen handed the keys over to Julia and told her that she could use her car.", "We are not going all the way to Kenting, but only as far as Kaohsiung.", "Jessica has/had no idea who put/had put the chocolate on her desk.", "It is important to learn lessons from your own mistakes.", "During the summer vacation, Joseph realized that he was wasting his life by doing nothing.", "Now, in order not to let his parents down, he has decided to study hard to get into a good college."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Jessica has/had no idea who put/had put the chocolate on her desk</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It is important to learn lessons from your own mistakes</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">During the summer vacation, Joseph realized that he was wasting his life by doing</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">nothing</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Now, in order not to let his parents down, he has decided to study hard to get into a</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">good college</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["It’s great to make new friends when you are traveling in a different country.", "However, if you want to make a good first impression, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) learning</strong> how to greet people will definitely help.", "After all, people in other countries often use greetings different from <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) our</strong> own.", "Here’s a well-known example from the Japanese.", "In Japan, bowing is the way <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (A) to say</strong> hello and show respect for others.", "The type of bow varies based on whom you are greeting.", "Some bows take <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) no</strong> longer than a second, while others seem like they’ll never end.", "To learn <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) how you should bow</strong> in every situation may take a visitor years.", "Another example is from Tibet, where there is a very surprising way to greet others.", "Visitors to Tibet soon <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) come</strong> to realize that sticking your tongue out is a kind of hello.", "This greeting <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) has existed</strong> for over a thousand years.", "It began as a way for monks to show that they weren’t the evil king Langdarma, whose tongue was known to be black.", "Though there is no need to prove it today, monks still quickly stick out their tongues to greet each other or to show agreement.", "Still another example is from Botswana; the greeting used there <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) looks</strong> the most difficult in the world.", "It <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (D) includes</strong> several complicated hand-holding gestures.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (C) However</strong>, the last one of these gestures is easy: Just pat your heart.", "If you can become skilled at this greeting, you can surely master any of them!"], "questions": [], "source": ["It’s great to make new friends when you are traveling in a different country. However, if you want to make a good first impression,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) learning</strong>   how to greet people will definitely help. After all, people in other countries often use greetings different from   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) our</strong>   own. Here’s a well-known example from the Japanese. In Japan, bowing is the way   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (A) to say</strong>   hello \nand show respect for others. The type of bow varies based on whom you are greeting. Some bows take   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) no</strong>   longer than a second, while others seem like they’ll never end. To learn   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) how you should bow</strong>   in every situation may take a visitor years. Another example is from Tibet, where there is a very surprising way to greet others. Visitors to Tibet soon   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (C) come</strong>   to realize that sticking your tongue out is a kind of hello. This greeting   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (B) has existed</strong>   for over a thousand years. It began as a way for monks to show that they weren’t the evil king Langdarma, whose tongue was known to be black. Though there is no need to prove it today, monks still quickly stick out their tongues to greet each other or to show agreement. Still another example is from Botswana; the greeting used there   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) looks</strong>   the most difficult in the world. It   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (D) includes</strong>   several complicated* hand-holding gestures.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (C) However</strong>  , the last one of these gestures is easy: Just pat your heart. If you can become skilled at this greeting, you can surely master any of them!", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["The handshake is a common method of greeting others around the world.", "However, just because everyone knows about it, that doesn’t mean it’s the same everywhere.", "In fact, the handshake can differ from country to country.", "The following are a few examples.", "In Mexico, a handshake isn’t just a handshake.", "Often, it comes with a hug as well, so don’t be afraid of physical contact.", "On the contrary, in the neighboring United States, the handshake doesn’t usually come with a hug.", "Instead, it should come with eye contact.", "Looking away while someone is shaking your hand might be seen as impolite or make you look like you’ve got something to hide.", "Eye contact also goes along with a handshake in Brazil, only with a slight difference.", "If a man shakes hands with a woman, he also kisses her on the cheek.", "The number of kisses depends on where you are in Brazil.", "However, wherever you are, it is always between one and three kisses.", "By contrast, men never shake hands with women in Morocco; they do so only with other men.", "Furthermore, in that country, a handshake should be soft, not firm, and one’s grip should be light.", "Whether you are traveling somewhere for business or for pleasure, be sure to look up the right way to shake hands there before you go.", "It could make all the difference."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ D ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the purpose of this passage?", "(A) To show how to make eye contact with others.", "(B) To offer a tip on how to hug a person.", "(C) To explain why one should kiss others when greeting them.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) To introduce different types of handshakes.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following statements is true?", "(A) Men kiss women while they are shaking hands in Mexico.", "(B) Men hug and shake hands with women in the US.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) Men shake hands only with men in Morocco.</strong>", "(D) Men shake hands with women and then look away in Brazil.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t3.\tWhat advice does the author give to travelers?", "(A) Take good care of their hands.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) Greet people in the right way.</strong>", "(C) Learn more about local cultures.", "(D) Try different ways of shaking hands."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["The Dog, the Rooster, and the Fox (adapted from Aesop’s Fables) Once upon a time, a dog and a rooster went on a trip together.", "One night, they decided to rest in a forest.", "So the rooster flew up into a tree and sat on a branch high above, while the dog slept below at the foot of the tree.", "When it was almost dawn, the rooster started to crow so loudly that he attracted a fox’s attention.", "The fox thought he could make a meal out of the bird.", "Therefore, he walked toward the tree and spoke to the rooster in the branches: “Because you sing so well and are such a useful bird to all living creatures, I would like to invite you to come down so that we can sing and have fun together.”", "“I think that is a good idea,” replied the rooster.", "“Come to the foot of the tree, my friend.”", "However, when the fox moved closer to the tree, he found that the dog was waiting there for him.", "Then the dog ended his life."], "questions": ["In the rooster’s smart (1)    <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">reply</strong>     to the fox, he avoided becoming the fox’s meal by (2) <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">inviting/attracting</strong>  the fox to move toward his partner, the dog.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are true for the animals in the story. \n     <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">C E F</strong>", "(A) The rooster and the dog took the trip to find food together.", "(B) The rooster crowed to attract the fox’s attention for the dog.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) The fox thought the rooster could be a delicious meal.</strong>", "(D) The rooster and the dog slept at the same place.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(E) The fox and the rooster lied to each other.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(F) The fox was killed by the dog in the end.</strong>", "3.\tWhich animal in the story is the “I” in the first paragraph? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">the fox</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "R02": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["Don’t feel upset about the failure.", "You should be more positive about what has happened.", "You’re obviously too tired to do any more work.", "You should take a nap.", "Kevin felt sorry about his behavior and promised not to drink too much again.", "The final exams are coming next week, so the library will be very crowded this weekend.", "We dressed up for Lily’s birthday party, but she was still in her ordinary clothes.", "The mother was wondering what had motivated her son to clean the whole house.", "Everyone thinks Robert is twenty-five, but actually, he is already thirty-five.", "Though the experiment isn’t going well at the moment, scientists are still very confident that it will succeed in the end.", "To avoid memory loss or other health problems, it is important for us to get enough sleep.", "The audience was disappointed that the famous singer refused to perform many of his old hit songs."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["Mr. Lee was given an award last month for his creative ways of teaching math.", "My boyfriend bought me many of my favorite skin-care products for my birthday.", "The mother told her kid that if he couldn’t behave himself in the store, they would have to leave.", "There is a promotion at the movie theater tonight.", "If you buy one ticket, you’ll get another one for free.", "Mary’s English is much better now, but there’s still room for improvement.", "She still needs to study hard."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["Cindy doesn’t let her disabilities stop her from doing the things she loves.", "Watching Hollywood movies on TV is my favorite pastime.", "You had better leave the house early (so as) to avoid missing the train.", "Because of Coach Cooper’s help, we could defeat the other team and win!", "The weather was so nice this weekend that many people went to the beach.", "These traditional clothes were made by the old men, who work eight hours a day.", "Ryder lost his Bluetooth earphones, which had cost him five thousand dollars.", "It was when Lily rushed out of the classroom that she bumped into Mrs. Jones.", "My elder brother, whom I admire a lot, is a well-known doctor."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Cindy doesn’t let her disabilities stop her from doing the things she loves</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Watching Hollywood movies on TV is my favorite pastime</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">You had better leave the house early (so as) to avoid missing the train</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Because of Coach Cooper’s help, we could defeat the other team and win</strong>!", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The weather was so nice this weekend that many people went to the beach</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">These traditional clothes were made by the old men, who work eight hours a day</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Ryder lost his Bluetooth earphones, which had cost him five thousand dollars</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was when Lily rushed out of the classroom that she bumped into Mrs. Jones</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">My elder brother, whom I admire a lot, is a well-known doctor</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["You should think it over before you take any action .", "On such a hot day, I’d like to have a cold drink rather/instead than/of hot coffee.", "The country put up a monument in honor of those who had died in the war.", "The situation is so bad now that everyone is eager to see a change for the better.", "It was thanks to your help that I could finally achieve my goal of visiting those tourist attractions.", "When Sherry was riding her bike across the street, she got hit by a speeding car.", "It was then that a woman who was passing by and saw what happened dialed/called 119."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The situation is so bad now that everyone is eager to see a change for the better</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was thanks to your help that I could finally achieve my goal of visiting those tourist \t\nattractions</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">When Sherry was riding her bike across the street, she got hit by a speeding car</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was then that a woman who was passing by and saw what happened dialed/called 119</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["Humans are creatures of habit.", "Hence, we don’t <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) always</strong> enjoy it when our daily routines are disrupted or when we have to take a different approach to something.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) Another</strong> reason we avoid change is that it often requires effort and commitment.", "This is especially true when it comes to changing our response to climate change.", "Reversing the damage <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) that</strong> human activity has done to our environment is going to require us to change how we live in many ways.", "First, we’ll need to avoid <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) using</strong> traditional fossil fuels.", "This might mean choosing public transport <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) over</strong> private vehicles or switching to cleaner energy sources.", "Second, we’ll probably also need to consume far fewer animal products, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (A) which</strong> include what we eat and wear.", "This will also greatly affect our life.", "Significant changes like these won’t be easy <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (A) to make</strong> because change can cause stress.", "Professor Griffon Pinchot, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) however</strong>, thinks we can heal the planet and have fun at the same time.", "He believes people can be inspired to make changes if they know they will become happier <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) by</strong> consuming less, working together, and caring more for the environment.", "Sadly, not enough has been done so far to prevent climate change.", "Can we change that?", "Absolutely!", "If we don’t, it could <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (D) turn out</strong> to be a disaster.", "After all, we only have one planet."], "questions": [], "source": ["Humans are creatures of habit. Hence, we don’t   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (C) always</strong>   enjoy it when our daily routines are disrupted or when we have to take a different approach to something.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (D) Another</strong>", null, "This is especially true when it comes to changing our response to climate change. Reversing the damage   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (B) that</strong>   human activity has done to our environment is going to require us to change how we live in many ways. First, we’ll need to avoid   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (B) using</strong>   traditional \nfossil fuels. This might mean choosing public transport   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) over</strong>   private vehicles or switching to cleaner energy sources. Second, we’ll probably also need to consume far fewer animal products,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (A) which</strong>   include what we eat and wear. This will also greatly affect our life.", "Significant changes like these won’t be easy   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (A) to make</strong>   because change can cause stress. Professor Griffon Pinchot,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (C) however</strong>  , thinks we can heal the planet and have fun at the same time. He believes people can be inspired to make changes if they know they will become happier   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) by</strong>   consuming less, working together, and caring more for the environment.", "Sadly, not enough has been done so far to prevent climate change. Can we change that? Absolutely! If we don’t, it could   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (D) turn out</strong>   to be a disaster. After all, we only have one planet.", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["One of the most famous inventors who has ever lived is Thomas Edison.", "Many of the things he created with the power of his mind are still used by people everywhere in their daily lives.", "We can say that his inventions have shaped the world we live in today.", "Edison was born in a small town in Ohio in 1847.", "As a child, he hated school.", "In fact, he attended school for only three months before he was kicked out.", "After that, he mostly learned by reading books on his own.", "In his free time, he loved to do scientific experiments, especially with chemicals.", "In his early twenties, Edison often did his experiments at his workplace.", "Sometimes, those experiments went wrong, causing damage to his workplace.", "However, in 1869, he had his first success, inventing a machine that could show the changing values of stocks in real time.", "By the 1870s, he had his own lab, a place where he could invent all day and every day.", "Over the next few years, he invented the record player and then the electric light bulb.", "He even invented the first motion picture, or movie, and made improvements to the paper that photos were printed on.", "His inventions touched almost every aspect of people’s lives.", "After a long and productive life, he passed away in 1931, leaving behind a legacy that will never be forgotten."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ B ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the passage mainly about?", "(A) Edison’s private life with his family.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(B) Edison’s life story and achievements.</strong>", "(C) Some inventions that changed the world.", "(D) The importance of scientific experiments.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t2.\tAccording to the passage, what is true about Edison?", "(A) He once earned his living as a doctor.", "(B) He didn’t attend school until he was 15.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) He enjoyed doing experiments in his leisure time.</strong>", "(D) He learned almost everything from his mother.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ A ）</strong>\t3.\tWhich of the following is NOT one of Edison’s inventions?", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(A) Photo paper.</strong>", "(B) The record player.", "(C) The motion picture.", "(D) The electric light bulb."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["Dear guests, We welcome you to our hotel and hope that you enjoy our sauna.", "Below, we compare our sauna with the onsen in your country.", "We hope that you have a wonderful holiday and enjoy the facilities at our hotel.", "Sauna Onsen Country of Origin Finland Japan Venue A closed steam room An open hot-spring bath Health Effects Boost your metabolism &amp; blood circulation.", "Boost your metabolism &amp; blood circulation.", "Soften your skin.", "Temperature Lower than 90 ºC.", "Around 40 ºC.", "Heat Source Wood, electricity, and gas Geothermal Time 10.15 minutes 10.15 minutes Do’s &amp; Don’ts Shower first.", "Towel allowed.", "Keep quiet when in the room.", "Shower afterward.", "Shower first.", "No towel when in the bath.", "Keep quiet when in the bath.", "No shower afterward."], "questions": ["The hotel encourages (1)  <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Japanese</strong>   travelers to use the in-hotel facilities through the comparison between their onsen and the sauna, which (2)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">originated</strong>    in Finland.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are true for the sauna or the onsen.\n      <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">A D F</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(A) Onsen offer their guests beautiful outdoor scenery to enjoy.</strong>", "(B) Saunas are good for softening the skin.", "(C) You should cover yourself with a towel in both venues.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) The temperature of a sauna can be higher than that of an onsen.</strong>", "(E) The heat sources of both saunas and onsen come from nature only.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(F) It’s a custom to take a shower after enjoying a sauna.</strong>", "3.\tWhich word in the text means “hot spring”? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">onsen</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}, "R03": {"文意字彙": {"pairs": ["The mother died at a young age.", "Her death was a real tragedy for the whole family.", "Andrew’s presentation on environmental protection offered us a clear picture of how to keep our earth green.", "The scientist did an experiment and recorded every step clearly in his notebook.", "In my country, there is an obvious contrast between life in the city and life in the countryside.", "We’ll have to put up with the noise from the construction site until the work is completed.", "The movie script Tony had written captured the interest of several movie producers.", "After the earthquake, a lot of food and medicine were quickly sent to the disaster area.", "Since more people are spending their holidays on the island, the local tourism industry is growing fast.", "Don’t waste time fighting over small matters.", "Instead, pay attention to more important things.", "Cora is very sensitive to other people’s feelings and is always aware of what’s happening around her."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "詞類變化": {"pairs": ["If one wants to study or work efficiently, he or she needs to learn good time management skills.", "Our planet has become polluted with all kinds of waste, such as plastic and chemicals.", "George enjoys camping, especially when the scenery is as impressive as he expected.", "Greg treated Linda to dinner to show his gratitude after she helped him get a great job.", "Though Sandra was seriously ill, she gradually recovered due to her strong will and effective treatment."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "句型練習": {"pairs": ["I go to the gym twice a week both to stay fit and to relieve stress.", "Edward only spent 60,000 NT dollars on/buying this used car.", "We should leave now so that we won’t miss the beginning of the movie.", "The old gentleman who greeted students at the school gate is the principal.", "It was after Woody graduated from senior high school that he moved to Australia.", "Audrey goes to yoga class twice a week so that she can stay healthy.", "This online course will teach you how to communicate well with deaf people.", "My digital camera was stolen (by someone) while I was watching the fireworks.", "Many studies have shown that regular exercise can keep you young and healthy."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I go to the gym twice a week both to stay fit and to relieve stress</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Edward only spent 60,000 NT dollars on/buying this used car</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">We should leave now so that we won’t miss the beginning of the movie</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">The old gentleman who greeted students at the school gate is the principal</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was after Woody graduated from senior high school that he moved to Australia</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Audrey goes to yoga class twice a week so that she can stay healthy</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">This online course will teach you how to communicate well with deaf people</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">My digital camera was stolen (by someone) while I was watching the fireworks</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Many studies have shown that regular exercise can keep you young and healthy</strong>."]}, "翻譯": {"pairs": ["It is sad to learn that my hometown is no longer the same as it was before.", "It tore at Neil’s heart to think about the destruction of many ancient pieces of art.", "Michael’s efforts finally paid off when he had got a scholarship to study abroad .", "Robert wandered about in front of the girl so that he could attract her attention.", "I’ll never forget the terrible typhoon which/that hit and caused serious damage to our community last month.", "It was while I was a freshman in college that I began to work at a convenience store.", "During that time, I learned how to get along with people and how to solve problems."], "questions": [], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">Robert wandered about in front of the girl so that he could attract her attention</strong>.", null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">I’ll never forget the terrible typhoon which/that hit and caused serious damage to our</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">community last month</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">It was while I was a freshman in college that I began to work at a convenience store</strong>.", null, null, "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">During that time, I learned how to get along with people and how to solve</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">problems</strong>."]}, "綜合測驗": {"pairs": ["There are many environmental problems highlighted in Chi Po-lin’s film, Beyond Beauty: Taiwan from Above.", "This documentary, for which Chi <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) spent</strong> years filming Taiwan from above, begins by showing Taiwan’s stunning scenery.", "However, like many other films, it then <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (C) takes</strong> a turn, and the “villains” appear.", "These villains, in this case, are people.", "It is through several scenes <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (A) that</strong> we see just how human activity is negatively impacting Taiwan’s environment.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) For example</strong>, in mountain areas, Chi’s camera highlights how planting more betel nut trees can lead to more landslides.", "In other scenes, we see what is <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) happening to</strong> Taiwan’s mountain villages, which are now always in danger due to the risk of both these landslides and earthquakes.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (B) Soon after</strong> those scenes, Chi’s camera finds Taiwan’s fish farms, which look beautiful from above.", "In fact, they <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (C) look like</strong> shining mirrors.", "However, these farms use up a lot of groundwater.", "Therefore, <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) instead of</strong> being good for the environment, they can actually cause the land to sink, as the narrator tells us.", "Later, Chi’s camera flies over some buildings related to Taiwan’s IT industry.", "The narrator then <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) makes</strong> us aware that the IT industry uses up to 16% of all the energy in Taiwan and produces toxic waste.", "We should be grateful <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (C) to</strong> Chi for helping us see these problems.", "Hopefully, we can soon find a way to solve them."], "questions": [], "source": ["There are many environmental problems highlighted in Chi Po-lin’s film, Beyond Beauty: Taiwan from Above. This documentary, for which Chi   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">1. (B) spent</strong>   years filming Taiwan from above, begins by showing Taiwan’s stunning* scenery. However, like many other films, it then   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">2. (C) takes</strong>   a turn, and the “villains*” appear. These villains, in this case, are people. It is through several scenes   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">3. (A) that</strong>   we see just how human activity is negatively impacting Taiwan’s environment.   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">4. (D) For example</strong>  , in mountain areas, Chi’s camera highlights how planting more betel nut* trees can lead to more landslides*. In other scenes, we see what is   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">5. (D) happening to</strong>   Taiwan’s mountain villages, which are now always in danger due to the risk of both these landslides and earthquakes.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">6. (B) Soon after</strong>   those scenes, Chi’s camera finds Taiwan’s fish farms, which look beautiful from above. In fact, they   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">7. (C) look like</strong>   shining mirrors. However, these farms use up a lot of groundwater. Therefore,   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">8. (A) instead of</strong>   being good for the environment, they can actually cause the land to sink, as the narrator tells us. Later, Chi’s camera flies over some buildings related to Taiwan’s IT industry. The narrator then   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">9. (B) makes</strong>   us aware that the IT industry uses up to 16% of all the energy in Taiwan and produces toxic* waste. We should be grateful   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">10. (C) to</strong>   Chi for helping us see these problems. Hopefully, we can soon find a way to solve them.", null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "閱讀測驗": {"pairs": ["Chi Po-lin’s great film, Beyond Beauty: Taiwan from Above, shows us that Taiwan is a beautiful place.", "However, the film also makes it clear that the island was facing serious environmental problems at the time of filming.", "Moreover, many of these problems, which Chi filmed between 2009 and 2012, are still very real today.", "One major problem highlighted in the film is that of the negative effects brought by hillside farming.", "Take betel nut farms, for example.", "Betel nut trees are widely grown in hilly areas in Taiwan.", "However, their roots do not go very deep into the soil.", "Therefore, when heavy rains come, these plants are unable to absorb water quickly or trap soil effectively, causing landslides to become more common.", "Another problem is wastewater.", "Sadly, many factories in Taiwan dump their untreated wastewater into rivers.", "For instance, the Tamsui River, which runs through Taipei City and New Taipei City, is polluted from raw sewage and wastewater from many factories.", "As the film shows, rivers like this flow from the mountains to the sea, taking all the factory pollution with them.", "All these harmful chemicals wind up in our ecosystem and harm every form of life.", "Sadly, Chi died in a helicopter crash in 2017.", "He may no longer be with us, but the lessons he hoped to teach us about our environment still remain."], "questions": ["<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ D ）</strong>\t1.\tWhat is the purpose of this passage?", "(A) To tell stories about how people live in Taiwan.", "(B) To warn people about the risk of using chemicals.", "(C) To give advice on how to make Taiwan a better place.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) To point out the seriousness of environmental problems.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t2.\tWhich of the following statements is true about betel nut trees?", "(A) They are widely grown in coastal areas.", "(B) Most of their roots go deep into the soil.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) They are one of the causes of landslides.</strong>", "(D) They can absorb water and trap soil well.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">（ C ）</strong>\t3.\tWhat is the third paragraph mainly about?", "(A) What substances are often found in rivers.", "(B) Where the Tamsui River flows into the sea.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(C) How wastewater has become a problem in Taiwan.</strong>", "(D) How factories dump their untreated wastewater."], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}, "混合題": {"pairs": ["A narrative story is often divided into five parts—the exposition, the rising action, the climax, the falling action, and the resolution.", "One type of narrative story is the fable.", "The main character in a fable is usually the one who learns a lesson.", "Now, read the story below and answer the questions that follow.", "The Lion and the Mouse (adapted from Aesop’s Fables) A lion was sleeping in the forest.", "Suddenly, a little mouse ran into him unexpectedly.", "In fright, the mouse tried to run away.", "However, while she was running across the lion’s nose, he woke up from his nap and captured the tiny creature with his huge paw, ready to kill her.", "“Spare me please!” begged the poor mouse.", "“If you let me go, someday I will repay you.”", "On hearing this, the lion was much amused.", "He didn’t think that he would need a mouse to help him.", "Yet, he let the mouse go in order to show his kindness.", "A few days later, while the lion was approaching his prey, he was caught in a hunter’s net.", "Unable to escape, the lion filled the forest with his angry roars.", "Recognizing the lion’s voice, the mouse followed this voice and soon found the lion struggling in the net.", "She found one of the huge ropes that bound the lion and gnawed it until it parted.", "Soon, the lion was free.", "“You laughed when I said I would repay you,” said the mouse.", "“Now you know that even a mouse can help a lion.”"], "questions": ["From the story, we can learn the lesson: Be (1)    <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">kind</strong>      to those who need your help as you never know when you might be (2)   <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">repaid</strong>     by them when you are faced with a difficulty or struggle.", "2.\tFrom (A) to (F) below, choose the ONES that are true for the story.       <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">D E</strong>", "(A) The lion pretended to sleep in order to catch the mouse as his prey.", "(B) The second paragraph provides the background information of the story.", "(C) The lion let the mouse go so that she could save his life in the future.", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(D) When the mouse begged the lion, he didn’t believe that her promise would come true.</strong>", "<strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">(E) The climax of this story occurs in the fourth paragraph.</strong>", "(F) The mouse gave a hand to the lion because she was scared by his roars.", "3.\tWhich word in the story means “bit or chewed repeatedly”? <strong class=\"teacher-answer inline-answer\">gnawed</strong>"], "source": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}}};